{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith","id":1296519,"title":"My reaction to Lilith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-13T15:02:17-07:00","id":1296519,"title":"My reaction to Lilith","content":"So I just finished reading the Heroes and Monsters section of the Lunar previews. Among other good and bad points, which II might get into elsewhere, one of the most profound reactions I had was to Lilith's writeup.<br /> Specifically the part where the Admiral..... was not a thing.<br /> At first, I thought this was a copout. Part of Lilith's story, for as long as I had known it, was about her relationship to D, how abuse influences social and mental health, and how recovery is a slow, tricky process, especially when nobody helps you out of a toxic relationship.<br /> And yet, I also felt.... relieved. Like finding out somebody you care about has, in fact, escaped a toxic relationship, and we never have to say his name ever again. Like we're moving on from something.<br /> Don't get me wrong, Lilith's story is still sad, but it's almost a ?comfortable? sadness?<br /> I'm just curious how everyone else felt about it, if anything.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T15:07:35-07:00","id":1296522,"title":"","content":"I'm fine with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T15:07:42-07:00","id":1296523,"title":"","content":"I guess because i\u2019ve been a fan since the 1E Core Book, this was a lot easier and less shocking for me, because I remember Lilith BEFORE her narrative was built around domestic abuse, and I appreciate the return of that story. I\u2019m not opposed to a thoughtful exploration of partner abuse and survival in the setting - but a) i\u2019m not convinced Desus and Lilith were that, and b) I think it should be with new characters rather than hijacking and overshadowing someone\u2019s existing story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T15:34:02-07:00","id":1296530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296523#post1296523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess because i\u2019ve been a fan since the 1E Core Book, this was a lot easier and less shocking for me, because I remember Lilith BEFORE her narrative was built around domestic abuse, and I appreciate the return of that story. I\u2019m not opposed to a thoughtful exploration of partner abuse and survival in the setting - but a) i\u2019m not convinced Desus and Lilith were that, and b) I think it should be with new characters rather than hijacking and overshadowing someone\u2019s existing story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this but I do think the relationship being an issue near the end was an important detail. Also, she's no longer &quot;one of the best martial artists in creation&quot; anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T18:20:02-07:00","id":1296551,"title":"","content":"I like this Lilith better. Desus really was overused in previous editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T19:26:57-07:00","id":1296560,"title":"","content":"Desus was a trash character, the details of whom truly added nothing of merit to the setting, much like many of the characters fleshed out in DotFA.<br /> <br /> The life of Lilith that was fleshed out pre-DotFA told an interesting story about a terrible, complicated relationship only prolonged with a magical, unbreakable bond, and DotFA made the smiling god-monster bound to Lilith...gross and frankly boring in a &quot;banality of evil&quot; way and seemingly written for mAxImUm EdGe in the same vein as a lot of old White Wolf stuff that also didn't age well for the same reasons.<br /> <br /> Good fucking riddance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T19:43:37-07:00","id":1296566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296560#post1296560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Desus was a trash character, the details of whom truly added nothing of merit to the setting, much like many of the characters fleshed out in DotFA.<br /> <br /> The life of Lilith that was fleshed out pre-DotFA told an interesting story about a terrible, complicated relationship only prolonged with a magical, unbreakable bond, and DotFA made the smiling god-monster bound to Lilith...gross and frankly boring in a &quot;banality of evil&quot; way and seemingly written for mAxImUm EdGe in the same vein as a lot of old White Wolf stuff that also didn't age well for the same reasons.<br /> <br /> Good fucking riddance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before DoTFA he was pretty good show of Solar how messed up he had become, swan attributed some hideous stuff like trading souls for favors with the fae, I would still prefer Desus despite the shadow of Dreams of the first age. Whether they should be together or not, well they weren't before. I'm not sure they should be again. <br /> <br /> Also, I will say while DotFA did go overboard, they didn't shy away from solars becoming monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T19:53:45-07:00","id":1296574,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m of two minds, on the one hand the flagrant abuse played for spectacle bugged me\u2014 on the other I kind of feel like the third edition kinda took what little complexity was present with the issue of the usurpation and stripped it out. It no longer, to me feels like a potentially justified action that did indeed curb the excesses of a hegemonically dominant and nigh omnipotent regime (albeit replacing it with a different imperialist hegemony restricted more by its lack of power than by Its commitment to moral behavior) and I feel like lillith\u2019s pure bliss, more or less happily married for a couple centuries backstory exemplifies that for me. <br /> <br /> It also kinda bugs me that she entered a centuries long fugue state because her man left her\u2014 its the sort of thing that you rarely see Hetero-male characters doing even in progressive fiction and a trope often ascribed to women. It\u2019s not a big deal though I guess and its a big improvement over the uncomfortable way her story was handled in 2E (especially DotFA).<br /> <br /> On the whole though I do like the character and the fact that they made her self imposed exile a gradual thing rather than an abrupt transition, allowing her to be important in the founding of the silver pact\u2014 even if not as important as some of the other elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T20:25:02-07:00","id":1296580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296574#post1296574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also kinda bugs me that she entered a centuries long fugue state because her man left her\u2014 its the sort of thing that you rarely see Hetero-male characters doing even in progressive fiction and a trope often ascribed to women.</div> </div> </div> </div>An interesting perspective. I would have said the opposite,though I suppose maybe my mind went to &quot;epic sulk&quot; more than &quot;fugue state&quot;. Any female characters in particular you were thinking of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T20:28:58-07:00","id":1296582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296574#post1296574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m of two minds, on the one hand the flagrant abuse played for spectacle bugged me\u2014 on the other I kind of feel like the third edition kinda took what little complexity was present with the issue of the usurpation and stripped it out. It no longer, to me feels like a potentially justified action that did indeed curb the excesses of a hegemonically dominant and nigh omnipotent regime (albeit replacing it with a different imperialist hegemony restricted more by its lack of power than by Its commitment to moral behavior) and I feel like lillith\u2019s pure bliss, more or less happily married for a couple centuries backstory exemplifies that for me.<br /> <br /> It also kinda bugs me that she entered a centuries long fugue state because her man left her\u2014 its the sort of thing that you rarely see Hetero-male characters doing even in progressive fiction and a trope often ascribed to women. It\u2019s not a big deal though I guess and its a big improvement over the uncomfortable way her story was handled in 2E (especially DotFA).<br /> <br /> On the whole though I do like the character and the fact that they made her self imposed exile a gradual thing rather than an abrupt transition, allowing her to be important in the founding of the silver pact\u2014 even if not as important as some of the other elders.</div> </div> </div> </div>People never moving on happens pretty often in fiction, most characters just don't have the opportunity to spend centuries not moving on (but conversely they also can't usually say the relationship they are mourning <i>lasted</i> centuries either). And usually their not moving on also involves them dealing with it in an amazingly unhealthy way on top of never finishing the dealing with of it. For a prominent plot central example involving a male from recently that is Naruto spoilers (select to view) we have<span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"> Obito Uchiha trying to destroy the world to turn reality into a dream world where the girl he loved never died</span> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">despite having decades to move on and being a grown ass man still yearning for a 12 year old </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">end spoilers</span>.<br /> <br /> Edit: Another less spoilery example is Robert Baratheon never getting over Lyanna Stark even decades later (and after siring numerous children and getting married to another woman)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 03-13-2019, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T20:49:20-07:00","id":1296589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296580#post1296580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An interesting perspective. I would have said the opposite,though I suppose maybe my mind went to &quot;epic sulk&quot; more than &quot;fugue state&quot;. Any female characters in particular you were thinking of?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who suffered mental breakdowns as a result of the actions or death of their partner or another male figure or who react with mental imbalance to events that male characters take in stride?<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra, Tamora, John Connor\u2019s mom in the second terminator movie, Emily Watsons character in breaking the waves, Ophelia (from hamlet), the character who is not Rebecca in Rebecca, the female lead in 13 reasons why, a whole bunch of female comic book villains, to many to mention (poison ivy depending on the incarnation, Harley Quinn), though to be fair male super villains get similar treatments, this is a scattered and poorly organized list.<br /> <br /> What I meant more is that reacting to tragic external stimuli with mental illness or behaivior often related with mental illness is something I feel happens more to female than male protagonists in fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","user":"JiveX","date":". 03-14-2019, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T21:59:56-07:00","id":1296598,"title":"","content":"I didn't read Lunars. Don't have it either. <br /> <br /> What did I miss?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T22:42:02-07:00","id":1296611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296598#post1296598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't read Lunars. Don't have it either.<br /> <br /> What did I miss?</div> </div> </div> </div> Short version they changed a 'classic' (in that the tale was rather iconic and an exemplar of the 2e mindset, for better or worse) character from a person that went rather insane from suffering horrific abuse at the hands of a monster, to a character struggling to cope from the end of a deeply unhealthy (though not explicitly abusive) relationship.<br /> <br /> The original story has her as the partner of the wildly abusive Desus, who at one point beats her so viciously she has a miscarriage. He controls her with solar charms so powerful they are basically mind-control, including one that would force her to kill herself. The new relationship is much more vague, in that Lilith and Andamani are said to have at one point been passionately in love, a love they fell out of but never left each other. When Andamani dies, Lilith abandons the world and lives for centuries as an owl. She comes out of the Fugue because she senses that her Solar mate has been reborn. Its never really stated, but this implies at the very least a highly-codependent relationship.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T22:58:30-07:00","id":1296614,"title":"","content":"For my own take, while I am not going to miss the abuse-as-shock factor that always pervaded Desus and Lilith in the past I do think that something has been lost. I don't really know if this was cannon, but I always played Desus when he appeared as very much being under the effect of his own charms. Desus himself can't quite comprehend that his whims might be wrong, in fact they must be right because he had them. It gave a sense of moral ambiguity to him since its hard to say how responsible someone is for actions they are incapable of assessing as wrong. This is why I also disliked the idea that the Silver Prince was Desus, because the Silver Prince is a cartoon-villain and completely undermines any thoughtful element that might have existed in the story.<br /> <br /> I didn't like DoTFA since it really did paint the Solars as irredemable monsters, when I think a more thoughtful alternative exists. I always saw the first age ending not because the Solars are inhuman, but because the very things that can make people great and heroic might also make them dangerous under the right circumstances. Desus for instance needs to be loved, by everyone all the time. This need for adulation drove him to do great things on behalf of his people, but eventually also led him to try to insulate himself from the idea that he is not universally adored. <br /> <br /> I agree that at the moment we don't really know the context that caused the Sidereals to end the First Age, but I hope that when we do its because the First Age was a time of god-kings that were dangerous because of how deeply human they were, as opposed to generic decadent monsters that delighted in cruelty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T23:22:56-07:00","id":1296615,"title":"","content":"To clarify: the description was that they had a happy union largely but that they lost some of the passion and both did things that hurt eachother (sort of a normal relationship hardly implied to be unhealthy) and when he died she gradually lost interest in the world to the point she used her magic to give herself the mind of a bird for s couple centuries. <br /> <br /> My objects, which aren\u2019t strong, have little to do with my missing the abuse angle and a slight annoyance that two of the major explicitly female shanaya are willfully inhuman and have to a degree \u201copted out\u201d or taking a meaningful role in the setting, and in lilliths case it\u2019s only the return of her lost love that gave her back the will to be a human again. It\u2019s just a bit prosaic to me. And I feel bad being negative because I don\u2019t feel negatively in general about her, I\u2019m just explaining a minor complaint. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296614#post1296614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For my own take, while I am not going to miss the abuse-as-shock factor that always pervaded Desus and Lilith in the past I do think that something has been lost. I don't really know if this was cannon, but I always played Desus when he appeared as very much being under the effect of his own charms. Desus himself can't quite comprehend that his whims might be wrong, in fact they must be right because he had them. It gave a sense of moral ambiguity to him since its hard to say how responsible someone is for actions they are incapable of assessing as wrong. This is why I also disliked the idea that the Silver Prince was Desus, because the Silver Prince is a cartoon-villain and completely undermines any thoughtful element that might have existed in the story.<br /> <br /> I didn't like DoTFA since it really did paint the Solars as irredemable monsters, when I think a more thoughtful alternative exists. I always saw the first age ending not because the Solars are inhuman, but because the very things that can make people great and heroic might also make them dangerous under the right circumstances. Desus for instance needs to be loved, by everyone all the time. This need for adulation drove him to do great things on behalf of his people, but eventually also led him to try to insulate himself from the idea that he is not universally adored. <br /> <br /> I agree that at the moment we don't really know the context that caused the Sidereals to end the First Age, but I hope that when we do its because the First Age was a time of god-kings that were dangerous because of how deeply human they were, as opposed to generic decadent monsters that delighted in cruelty.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree there is a happy medium\u2014 but I also think even absent the great curse, A person given unlimited power and a lifespan in the millennia will inevitably become at the very least inhuman in their outlook and also very likely incredibly dangerous to humans around them\u2014 like how even very compassionate human\u2019s are dangerous to insects. Kind of always felt this \u201cring of gyges\u201d angle was missed. Still sort of feel that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T00:28:42-07:00","id":1296619,"title":"","content":"I think that this new Lilith's depression following the death of her Solar mate is less about her loosing him and more about the unresolved issues they had at the end that would never be resolved. It is like having a huge argument with a beloved family member where both you and them said and did things that seemed perfectly rational at the time (even if it was very much heat of the moment) but afterwards, with some time to think things through one begins to realize that it may not have been the best way to have gone about it. Of course, you think you will have time to go back and set things right in a few days or weeks... only to learn that any chance at a resolution has been lost because they have passed away suddenly and unexpectedly.<br /> <br /> The fact that there were fights, lies and betrayals near the end suggest that when he died, things had been left unresolved and that the longer she continued to fight those who murdered the one she had loved for so long... in all the places they had defended... the more the unresolved issues of that relationship began to remind her of all that she had lost... and maybe not for the best of reasons. What does a hurt pride really matter when one is faced with what can only be described as an eternity alone because of it? Does she regret not being there to maybe save her beloved... or not having died with her mate? She has survived because that is what she does... but was that survival worth the price?<br /> <br /> Now with her beloved's rebirth, she might have a chance of getting some closure and finally letting these old wounds heal at last... maybe even rekindle what she once had if possible. She doesn't know what she will find... and it may end up being all for naught... but better to know one way or the other than to constantly wonder what might have been. She had been down that road once before... and it seems she is now eager not to make the same mistakes twice.<br /> <br /> At least this is what I am seeing from this write up for her. Simply put... she didn't break down because she lost her love... but because she lost any chance (that she knew of) of resolving the issues they had left unresolved because of her mate's death. Regret and self-doubt can be just as crippling as any wound inflicted by a weapon... sometimes more so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T00:46:36-07:00","id":1296622,"title":"","content":"It's of note that in Lilith's statblock, her feelings towards Andamani are 'ambivalence'. She's not straightforwardly happy he's back, she's ambivalent, but his rebirth has stirred her enough to take action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T02:22:48-07:00","id":1296631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296574#post1296574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m of two minds, on the one hand the flagrant abuse played for spectacle bugged me\u2014 on the other I kind of feel like the third edition kinda took what little complexity was present with the issue of the usurpation and stripped it out. It no longer, to me feels like a potentially justified action that did indeed curb the excesses of a hegemonically dominant and nigh omnipotent regime (albeit replacing it with a different imperialist hegemony restricted more by its lack of power than by Its commitment to moral behavior) and I feel like lillith\u2019s pure bliss, more or less happily married for a couple centuries backstory exemplifies that for me.<br /> <br /> It also kinda bugs me that she entered a centuries long fugue state because her man left her\u2014 its the sort of thing that you rarely see Hetero-male characters doing even in progressive fiction and a trope often ascribed to women. It\u2019s not a big deal though I guess and its a big improvement over the uncomfortable way her story was handled in 2E (especially DotFA).<br /> <br /> On the whole though I do like the character and the fact that they made her self imposed exile a gradual thing rather than an abrupt transition, allowing her to be important in the founding of the silver pact\u2014 even if not as important as some of the other elders.</div> </div> </div> </div>My biggest issue is that this presents the situation as either lunars were okay with solars being monsters and didn't care about the situation that was happening when compared to the rather neutral text of the solars were becoming monsters and the sidereals and dragon blooded rose up in the core. It's kind of confirming that it seems like no lunar actually had an issue with how solars were acting before the usurpation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T04:26:06-07:00","id":1296644,"title":"","content":"Mmm....<br /> <br /> I do not object to changing Lilith as a matter of principal. While on the whole I stand behind 2e, if you're going to be making setting modifications this is something I agree is worth consideration, much like Lillun. DotFA harped on about how controlled she was, and defining her only in that light makes her more object than individual. This is something that is <i>very </i>open to improvement.<br /> <br /> But as someone who hadn't read a pre-DotFA portrayal of Lilith before? This did not sell me on her as a cool or interesting character. I don't really get what the idea here was. She was in love with a guy in the first age, after he died she withdrew from the world, now he's back and she... might do something? I don't feel this makes her a better character. More useable in a FA Romance plot, sure, and a good 'basic' example of that, but for someone who doesn't particularly care for that side of the setting this is uncompelling.<br /> <br /> Also am I the only one uncomfortable with the fact that this new Lilith is basically how Desus envisioned her in the old continuity? Her life revolved around her mate and without him she retreated from the world. As problematic as the old take was, you could cast her life as an owl as one of freedom and self empowerment, rather than this which makes it more... depressing, frankly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T04:52:52-07:00","id":1296650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296574#post1296574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m of two minds, on the one hand the flagrant abuse played for spectacle bugged me\u2014 on the other I kind of feel like the third edition kinda took what little complexity was present with the issue of the usurpation and stripped it out. It no longer, to me feels like a potentially justified action that did indeed curb the excesses of a hegemonically dominant and nigh omnipotent regime (albeit replacing it with a different imperialist hegemony restricted more by its lack of power than by Its commitment to moral behavior) and I feel like lillith\u2019s pure bliss, more or less happily married for a couple centuries backstory exemplifies that for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that has a lot more to do with what's been getting focus than statements on the legitimacy of Ex3's Usurpation. There's no attempt made by the Dragon-Blooded material to legitimise their rebellion because to them its ancient history. We're going to have to see what the Bronze Faction has to say for themselves when the time comes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T05:00:31-07:00","id":1296653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296644#post1296644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">much like Lillun..</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the little girl who sits in a well furnished room with plenty of games and companions while her unique soul harbors some exaltations? A little girl who isn't <i><b>in any way</b></i> a mass of tentacles and suffering? because that's how she's always been. <br /> <br /> Always. <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">ALWAYS. </span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T05:16:37-07:00","id":1296657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296653#post1296653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">because that's how she's always been. <br /> <br /> Always. <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">ALWAYS. </span></b></div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer <i>Aspect Book: Earth</i>'s take on her - she disappears while sneaking into the Imperial Manse after the Scarlet Empress, at the behest of Mnemon, and possesses no connection to the Infernal Exalted whatsoever.<br /> <br /> For all we know, she's Daenerys Stormborn, sent across the sea to hide her from the vicious backbiting politics on the main continent. <br /> <br /> Or maybe she remained in the Imperial Manse, and when the Solars imprisoned there broke out, they took her under their wing, not knowing she's the child of the Scarlet Empress.<br /> <br /> Or maybe she's dead. But hey, there's options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-14-2019, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T07:31:24-07:00","id":1296689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296589#post1296589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who suffered mental breakdowns as a result of the actions or death of their partner or another male figure or who react with mental imbalance to events that male characters take in stride?</div> </div> </div> </div>ACHILLES.<br /> <br /> Maybe Herakles?<br /> <br /> Frank Castle, the Punisher.<br /> <br /> Batman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 03-14-2019, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T07:35:39-07:00","id":1296690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296650#post1296650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that has a lot more to do with what's been getting focus than statements on the legitimacy of Ex3's Usurpation. There's no attempt made by the Dragon-Blooded material to legitimise their rebellion because to them its ancient history. We're going to have to see what the Bronze Faction has to say for themselves when the time comes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. Justifying the imperialism of the Scarlet Dynasty would be much more relevant to the living generations of Creation. It's also impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T07:42:22-07:00","id":1296692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296650#post1296650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that has a lot more to do with what's been getting focus than statements on the legitimacy of Ex3's Usurpation. There's no attempt made by the Dragon-Blooded material to legitimise their rebellion because to them its ancient history. We're going to have to see what the Bronze Faction has to say for themselves when the time comes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, for the Dragonblooded the usurpation happened like 1400 years ago, that\u2019s like 24 dragon blooded generations ago (given their extended lifespan) that\u2019s like saying people in America don\u2019t study Columbus\u2019s arrival because it\u2019s ancient history. Though I take your point, the Immaculates don\u2019t do a lot of \u201creasoning\u201d and instead take a more dictatorial ideological tact. I just think that it seems a bit silly, givent that the terrestrial book is filled with stories about how terrestrials and the realm are corrupt/mismanaging things, they didn\u2019t bother including examples of celestial behavior that could even be pointed at by an extremist to legitimize their treatment of solars as anathema. The lunars book certainly contained a fair bit of material on lunar monstrosity at the character level, don\u2019t get me wrong, speaking more from the perspective that basically everyone still alive at the time thought the usurpation was a horrible missdead even though it\u2019s referenced in lunars that some lunars were on the Bronze faction\u2019s side. Where\u2019s my deeply conflicted lunar elder, who\u2019s inmbeded herself in the powerstructures of the Immaculate Faith or the Realm Deliberative desguised as different dynasts since day one, hoping to curb the worst of its excesses or hold it together?<br /> <br /> Not suggesting that literally should be a character, just that variance is fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","user":"JiveX","date":". 03-14-2019, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T07:49:28-07:00","id":1296693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296689#post1296689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ACHILLES.<br /> <br /> Maybe Herakles?<br /> <br /> Frank Castle, the Punisher.<br /> <br /> Batman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Achilles is a good example, but his epic sulk is notable because of how rare that sort of behavior was for Greek heroes. Lilith vanishes and no one cares, no-one comes to her tent to tell she owes it to her fledgling nation to get some help, she is so alone and isolated from lunar society at the point that she exists it (slowly) that everyone forgets about her? <br /> <br /> The Punjsher just goes on a revenge spree (if I\u2019m correct right) that\u2019s not really mental breakdown in the same way that giving oneself the brain of an owl so as to become physically incapable of experiencing emotions is. It\u2019s also well within the cannon of \u201cappropriate male motivations in fiction that are actually highly problematic when played out in the real world\u201d. I do agree there are lots more examples in comics on both sides than seems reasonable though, Greek myths too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","user":"JiveX","date":". 03-14-2019, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T08:12:39-07:00","id":1296699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296693#post1296693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Achilles is a good example, but his epic sulk is notable because of how rare that sort of behavior was for Greek heroes. Lilith vanishes and no one cares, no-one comes to her tent to tell she owes it to her fledgling nation to get some help, she is so alone and isolated from lunar society at the point that she exists it (slowly) that everyone forgets about her?<br /> <br /> The Punjsher just goes on a revenge spree (if I\u2019m correct right) that\u2019s not really mental breakdown in the same way that giving oneself the brain of an owl so as to become physically incapable of experiencing emotions is. It\u2019s also well within the cannon of \u201cappropriate male motivations in fiction that are actually highly problematic when played out in the real world\u201d. I do agree there are lots more examples in comics on both sides than seems reasonable though, Greek myths too.</div> </div> </div> </div>*nods* Trying to put a bow on this, male heroes when responding to tragedy get active reactions. Punisher, Batman, Achilles, whoever: the tragic events inspire them to do stuff and become characters in their own right. Lilith is inspired to <i>not </i>act by her tragedy in contrast. That's rare but what few examples I can think of for it are female. Miss Havisham, if you'll permit a classic, seems a depressingly on point comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T08:19:49-07:00","id":1296702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296693#post1296693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lilith vanishes and no one cares\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is a remotely charitable read of the situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296693#post1296693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">no-one comes to her tent to tell she owes it to her fledgling nation to get some help\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>1) There's a difference between &quot;they didn't succeed,&quot; and &quot;they didn't try.&quot; Nothing implies the latter.<br /> 2) It's not presented as if the second he died, she decided to spend 100% of her time as an owl; she gradually eased into it as the pillars of her old life fell away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T08:33:44-07:00","id":1296704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296699#post1296699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *nods* Trying to put a bow on this, male heroes when responding to tragedy get active reactions. Punisher, Batman, Achilles, whoever: the tragic events inspire them to do stuff and become characters in their own right. Lilith is inspired to <i>not </i>act by her tragedy in contrast. That's rare but what few examples I can think of for it are female. Miss Havisham, if you'll permit a classic, seems a depressingly on point comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh how did I forget that one! And yes, to not act or else act in a way that is self negating. (Exile, suicide, withdrawal from public life, turning into an owl, etc)<br /> <br /> Count alucard:<br /> If something isn\u2019t mentioned in a backstory, it is reasonable to assume it didn\u2019t happen or if it did wasn\u2019t a significant part of the story. However, to your point, I agree I am overstating my point; Even reading it now it\u2019s not nessecarily reflective of how I feel holistically about the character, just me trying to clarify my limited objections. Sometimes I express things too strongly in one direction when I do that \u2014 so let me walk it back; Lilith Is much improved in this edition, something about her turning into an owl for several centuries smacks of an abjedecation of agency which, for reasons of common presentations of normative gender behavior in fiction, feels a bit more annoying to me on Lilith than it did on say leviathan. Also, as far as I can tell of the mentioned ancient (first age lunars) only three (Raksi, Lillith and Rhadika) are women explicitly and of them two have had serious bouts of mental illness or similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","user":"JiveX","date":". 03-14-2019, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T08:49:21-07:00","id":1296705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296598#post1296598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did I miss?</div> </div> </div> </div>A damned fine read.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296704#post1296704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If something isn\u2019t mentioned in a backstory, it is reasonable to assume it didn\u2019t happen or if it did wasn\u2019t a significant part of the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that &quot;Someone tried to convince me to come back, but they weren't very convincing&quot; would indeed be pretty insignificant in Lillith's story, considering it takes place over more than a thousand years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-14-2019, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T09:35:28-07:00","id":1296723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296631#post1296631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest issue is that this presents the situation as either lunars were okay with solars being monsters and didn't care about the situation that was happening when compared to the rather neutral text of the solars were becoming monsters and the sidereals and dragon blooded rose up in the core. It's kind of confirming that it seems like no lunar actually had an issue with how solars were acting before the usurpation.</div> </div> </div> </div>3e has, to me, been very &quot;real politik&quot; about the Usurpation. It was at it's core, a regime change. And regime changes, at their core, are ugly, with a lot of different intersts, contradicting incentives, and so on. Part of this is that many people may have been complicit with a previosu regime, and while not agreeing with its details, are kind of pissed they were not brought to the table when said regime change was brought about.<br /> <br /> Note, the Introduction outright says Lunars did kill their Solar mates in the fray. It's just that for any given DB, Lunars were so part of the Solar hegemony, it's not clear that for many whether it was genuinely them being on the uprising's side, or opportunism. It might ahave been both. And again, in regime changes, it often doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> And also as stated, right now, that was fifteen centuries ago. The actual actors are mostlyd ead, and the actual folks involved in a lot of the Lunar war on the Realm are thos born in its aftermath. Whether Lunars careda bout the Solar corruption or not is moot, as a lot of the stuff since is about the fallout more than the reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T09:41:47-07:00","id":1296726,"title":"","content":"The possibility of lunar conspirators still alive and hiding among the dragon blooded is one to think about, that's for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T09:44:46-07:00","id":1296727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296705#post1296705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A damned fine read.<br /> <br /> I'd argue that &amp;quot;Someone tried to convince me to come back, but they weren't very convincing&amp;quot; would indeed be pretty insignificant in Lillith's story, considering it takes place over more than a thousand years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Goddamn it. Should I buy it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T09:48:42-07:00","id":1296730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296727#post1296727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Goddamn it. Should I buy it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes. You only have like an hour to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T10:43:50-07:00","id":1296740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296730#post1296730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes. You only have like an hour to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh... too much work. Nevermind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T11:10:30-07:00","id":1296750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296730#post1296730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes. You only have like an hour to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ll second this! Despite my minor nit picks with certain parts (there are a couple charms I dont love because I think they uncomplicate certain combat options in an un-fun way, mostly the immovability charm and the auto knockback charm and besides Lilith there are a few characters I would rather have seen done differently and certain angles I would have liked to see explored\u2014 I mentioned one above\u2014 that just weren\u2019t) I absolutely love lunars In 3E. I\u2019m not coming at this like @sunderthegold as someone who always loved lunars even when they barely showed any of the traits that I loved about them (forgive the oversimplification). They were far and away my least favorite splat in both editions, I found them dull and boring and uninspired, and this edition I find my opinions totally reversed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T11:18:18-07:00","id":1296753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296692#post1296692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, for the Dragonblooded the usurpation happened like 1400 years ago, that\u2019s like 24 dragon blooded generations ago (given their extended lifespan)</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Realm era, the majority of Dragon Blooded barely live to a hundred. I presume that might go double for the extreme violence of the Shogunate.<br /> <br /> Practically speaking, the longevity of the Terrestrial Exalted comes out less as them having fewer generations, and more as them having generations of regular length in which almost everybody stays pretty until misadventure, intrigue or war takes them, and at big family gatherings there'll be a few venerable fossils who'll command a lot of attention, but probably be too busy or important for you to talk to them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T11:26:22-07:00","id":1296754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296753#post1296753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the Realm era, the majority of Dragon Blooded barely live to a hundred. I presume that might go double for the extreme violence of the Shogunate.<br /> <br /> Practically speaking, the longevity of the Terrestrial Exalted comes out less as them having fewer generations, and more as them having generations of regular length in which almost everybody stays pretty until misadventure, intrigue or war takes them, and at big family gatherings there'll be a few venerable fossils who'll command a lot of attention, but probably be too busy or important for you to talk to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point remains. People in the 1600\u2019s studied events well before the current era and their average life expectancy was half that\u2014 even not accounting for high mortality in youth. It doesn\u2019t matter that most terrestrials don\u2019t make it past 100 the ones that do are the social movers and shakers of the culture and therefore would inform the academic discourse. It\u2019s just not, to me, realistic that this subject wouldn\u2019t come up even though there would be people alive for most of the shogunate and many years of the early realm whose parents or grandparents rememebered the usurpation.<br /> <br /> Also, per the core, the average life expectancy is 250-300 years\u2014 so not sure where less than a hundred is coming from. (Ex3 34)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","user":"JiveX","date":". 03-14-2019, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T11:37:45-07:00","id":1296758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296631#post1296631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest issue is that this presents the situation as either lunars were okay with solars being monsters and didn't care about the situation that was happening when compared to the rather neutral text of the solars were becoming monsters and the sidereals and dragon blooded rose up in the core. It's kind of confirming that it seems like no lunar actually had an issue with how solars were acting before the usurpation.</div> </div> </div> </div>An impression I'm getting from these write-ups is that, when it comes right down to it, the surviving First Age Lunars are a bit self-involved. Ma-Ha-Suchi is motivated partially because he wants a new Realm to be acclaimed in, Raksi has a Defining Tie to herself, Seven Obsidian Leopard spends a lot of time hanging out with ancient ghosts and spirits of violence, and, while Lilith's backstory is certainly compelling and sympathetic, I'm ultimately reading it less as severe trauma and more as fantastical melodrama.<br /> <br /> The impression I get from this is that the Solar and Lunar Exalted of the final days of the First Age were collectively somewhat... insulated by their stature, the grandiosity of their lifestyles, the available means for the world to be a grand adventure. It's all intense relationships and overwrought emotions for them. For the Lunars specifically, not just because of the manner in which they're so deeply intertwined with the Solars, but also one another, through that iteration of the Silver Pact.<br /> <br /> I think it's reasonable, under those circumstances, for them to have a distinct difficulty with objectivity. I think it's even more reasonable when, rather than give them the chance, their fellow Exalted independently make the decision to slaughter the Solars and destroy the Realm; unobjective enough to not fully consider how some of that destruction is not entirely on them, when there's infrastructure created to outright rebel (or at least does so as an unforeseen consequence).<br /> <br /> It wouldn't be unreasonable to assume that even a Lunar who did have a less invested perspective in the Solars and the Realm would still join the cause against the Usurpers, because they didn't exactly make a good show as a replacement.<br /> <br /> I don't doubt that a First Age elder who is more cloistered from the Pact because they can't really fault the Sidereals and Dragon Blooded for their actions and look warily on how their fellows might govern if they win would make for a compelling and believable individual character. But I don't fault the absence of such amidst a lot of other characters that need to be put in, and don't think the most ancient Lunars come across too poorly in this world of grand melodrama and high-flying kung fu action that the response to your query is &quot;yes, but&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T11:49:44-07:00","id":1296761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296753#post1296753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the Realm era, the majority of Dragon Blooded barely live to a hundred. I presume that might go double for the extreme violence of the Shogunate.<br /> <br /> Practically speaking, the longevity of the Terrestrial Exalted comes out less as them having fewer generations, and more as them having generations of regular length in which almost everybody stays pretty until misadventure, intrigue or war takes them, and at big family gatherings there'll be a few venerable fossils who'll command a lot of attention, but probably be too busy or important for you to talk to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this. I feel like we sometimes drag our modernity screaming and kicking into this when we talk about perspectives and lifestyles in Creation (largely about life expectancy, politics and diet).<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded are Exalted, Classical heroes who wouldn't be out of place in any mythic cycle. How often do heroes in just about any given mythology die of old age? Or even make it to middle age for that matter?<br /> <br /> Several sources have said multiple times that not that many Dragon-Blooded make it to retirement age, and many of those are lost in their early years when Essence fever and the arrogance of youth are married to literal superpowers. Creation is dangerous enough on a default level and Exalts are typically ones to <i>actively </i>seek out things that can plausibly hurt them. This is all before one accounts for the fact that DBs are born into a premodern ruling class which is still human enough to be deathtrap of intrigue.<br /> <br /> I also hate to bring this up, but not that many historical empires, countries or civilizations felt any great need to justify their success along any sort of empathetic criteria. They might concern themselves with how it might be justified by the perspectives of their own culture, but they are not going to feel terribly bad about having won. Any Realm scholar writing the history of a recently conquered Satrapy could easily use the notes of Bronze Faction writers as a pretty solid guideline, so I do not think that comparing a DB learning about something a similar number of generations ago automatically means they will study it in the exact same fashion.<br /> <br /> On the Lilith note, my reaction was positive but it brought up a question to my mind. Lilith was already old when the Usurpation came (in as much as that has meaning to an Exalt), she and her mate had gone through an immense number of good and bad times together by the time one died. I find the 'her man left' or 'love interest axed' angles to be a bit odd in that context, if only because the following sentences went into detail about her Shogunate activities, but I am intrigued about that idea of time.<br /> <br /> I can't speak for everyone but I assume most people have seen what happens when one half of a senior couple dies, more often than not it breaks the remaining half in my experience. Even those that cope are left changed by it and often develop some odd quirks (I vividly remember my grandmother sometimes talking as if my grandfather was still alive a decade after his passing) because it is <i>hard </i>to lose someone who you have literally built your life with. An Exalt can't grow old and I do not think their bodies can fail them the way ours can in old age. What happens to even the strongest of spirits when that grief, that scale of loss, wears down on you but your body refuses to let you rest?<br /> <br /> Don't know, maybe all that some can see is the character being insufficiently strong or being subsumed by something she should just 'get over', But I sort of see the equivalent of what happens when your partner of fifty years leaves first, while your own body and the world carry on without giving you time to put the pieces back together.<br /> <br /> Or maybe I am just expecting Exalted not to be just about unchanging 20-30 somethings who dont age mentally and can revert to default at the speed of a comic book superhero<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Either way, Vance and Minton have really made 3ed into a truly lovely thing and I am happier with every new piece they give me for me and my players to explore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 03-14-2019, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T12:00:59-07:00","id":1296764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296754#post1296754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">even not accounting for high mortality in youth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly speaking, that shouldn't be accounted for. Infant mortality being incorporated into life expectancy averages seems to generate certain misconceptions about how long people lived, when it's closer to accurate to say that people in general could live to reasonable old age, it's just that there were a lot fewer of them around because living past infancy was more difficult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s just not, to me, realistic that this subject wouldn\u2019t come up even though there would be people alive for most of the shogunate and many years of the early realm whose parents or grandparents rememebered the usurpation.</div> </div> </div> </div>But do they remember it academically, or politically?<br /> <br /> I wonder how many elderly German people within the last few decades have accurately remembered their actions and perspectives during the 30s and 40s.<br /> <br /> {tries to remember course of discussion}<br /> <br /> And as this is a point about the presentation in their respective books, I would point out that your statements are still begging a question of whether or not the knowledge being present is equivalent to it being significant.<br /> <br /> If you say that people in the 1600s knew of older, even ancient, history, my question is <i>which</i> people? Many people? Important people? And if important, did it still heavily inform policies of the day?<br /> <br /> That information concerning the specifics of the Usurpation is available to the academically inclined Dynast does not mean that such is very important with their overall society, faced as it is with the difficulties of ruling their empire. It's not important to their day to day lives. Even if their own generations were at the maximum length, more than a thousand years would not be equivalent to a couple hundred of them, because there's still more stuff happening in that time; not just to the mortal societies that exist around them, but within their own lives.<br /> <br /> Living to three hundred years doesn't mean you experience that time as though it was seventy years, it means you've got to cope with enough events to make up about four lifetimes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, per the core, the average life expectancy is 250-300 years\u2014 so not sure where less than a hundred is coming from. (Ex3 34)</div> </div> </div> </div>Under the circumstances, I think it's best to read that in terms of the average lifespan that Dragon Blooded <i>could</i> have lived had they not been killed. Like, the maximum lifespan their biology can afford them. Both prior Editions were consistent with the idea that few Dynasts actually survived to old age, they just didn't put a number to it. What Fire Has Wrought had a few issues to deal with, so they did, and that number was about a century, with Dynasts teetering at old age being a distinct minority.<br /> <br /> And generally engaged in more practical business than academia.<br /> <br /> For outcastes, I've personally got an image in which it's hard for most of them to actually make it out of childhood, but that largely reflects my fascination with the instabilities of the teenage brain combined with the revision saying that, regardless of their breeding, most Dragon Blooded Exalt in early adolescence. Setting that aside, the number of those who survive to old age definitely has to be even more of a marked minority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T12:08:21-07:00","id":1296766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296693#post1296693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Achilles is a good example, but his epic sulk is notable because of how rare that sort of behavior was for Greek heroes. Lilith vanishes and no one cares, no-one comes to her tent to tell she owes it to her fledgling nation to get some help, she is so alone and isolated from lunar society at the point that she exists it (slowly) that everyone forgets about her?</div> </div> </div> </div>Achilles sulked in his tent, THEN his lover dies, then he goes on a rampage, then he dies.<br /> <br /> Lillith's lover died, THEN she goes on a rampage, but then she doesn't die. She fights, and fights, and fights, but she never gets what she really wants, since nothing brings her lover back to her, and anything or anyone else that might motivate her also dies or vanishes, so she gradually takes longer and longer vacations, and before the Solars returned, she and all of her peers were so old that her current vacation didn't seem particularly prolonged. They all still considered her part of the Silver Pact; just taking a well-deserved sabbatical.<br /> <br /> Ma-Ha-Suchi had a similar experience, where after the heirs of the Shogunate survived and built a new empire after the Fair Folk Invasion, he just sort of gave up for a bit.<br /> <br /> I forget why Leviathan is considered different, but the Pact at large seems to think he was a coward who didn't help when he should, and Sha Oka'a resents him for it.<br /> <br /> Raksi's experience differed from Lilith's in that Raksi was interested in building a domain to rule as queen, which clearly didn't interest Lilith at all. Lilith's hobbies didn't involve building anything that required constant investment and management.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 03-14-2019, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T12:31:54-07:00","id":1296774,"title":"","content":"I just want to say that I understand where JiveX is coming from with that side of Lilith's concept. Even when there might be cases of something roughly equivalent for masculine characters, there's a background that gives them both certain connotations that are different.<br /> <br /> If Lilith was a character wholly new to the Edition, I might roll my eyes at it, but she was a certain weight of legacy from the early parts of the game, and that combined with how the concept of her having sequestered herself from her pain in an owl shape for centuries is something I find compelling leads me to file her under &quot;problematic, but with worthwhile elements&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T14:10:53-07:00","id":1296788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296774#post1296774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want to say that I understand where JiveX is coming from with that side of Lilith's concept. Even when there might be cases of something roughly equivalent for masculine characters, there's a background that gives them both certain connotations that are different.<br /> <br /> If Lilith was a character wholly new to the Edition, I might roll my eyes at it, but she was a certain weight of legacy from the early parts of the game, and that combined with how the concept of her having sequestered herself from her pain in an owl shape for centuries is something I find compelling leads me to file her under &amp;quot;problematic, but with worthwhile elements&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate that and for what it\u2019s worth I\u2019m largely on the same page. <br /> <br /> I am curious where in the terrestrial book they talk about life expectancy, having trouble finding it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T14:17:49-07:00","id":1296789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296788#post1296788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am curious where in the terrestrial book they talk about life expectancy, having trouble finding it</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be the &quot;Generations in the Dynasty&quot; sidebar found on page 100 of What Fire Has Wrought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T19:23:21-07:00","id":1296866,"title":"","content":"Well... I will say, claiming Lilith plays too much into a gendered trope doesn't really hold merit with me. From both personal experience with friends going through a similar phase after a bitter divorce, as well as the fictional references others have pointed out, making a character that struggles with loss is almost mandatory for a splat that prides itself on its deep personal bond themes and characters that survived multiple bloodbath incidents.<br /> <br /> To reduce such a thing as an eye-roller is basically eye roll worthy in itself for me.<br /> <br /> As for DotFA, I'm probably in the minority that loved it for contributing to the whacky over the top charm 2E had for me. I am truly sad to see the line depart from another of many things that brought me to love this game and this hobby as a whole. I'm sad to see Desus go, and I don't really have a good reason to embrace the new story as I will concede that it is a bit generic and overall &quot;meh&quot; both in its impact on the reader and literally in the intimacy write up for the character herself. Though I s'pose for a character centuries into the mourning process, &quot;meh&quot; is probably a vast improvement from the starting point.<br /> <br /> Perhaps my feelings will change as more stories are told, much as they have after playing with some of the new mechanics this edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13326-aredin","name":"Aredin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T20:01:28-07:00","id":1296873,"title":"","content":"A thing being realistic in particular cases does not mean that there aren't issues with recurring patterns to its depiction in art or culture, particularly when those depictions can end up being framed in a manner that adheres to harmful stereotypes.<br /> <br /> Even in cases where those things are surrounded by alternative examples that help to soften the impact with a more diverse range of characters, sometimes a trope can have a bad enough history that using it in any fashion can create at least uncomfortable recollections.<br /> <br /> As a different example of a similar phenomenon to illustrate my point: the setting of Exalted contains a variety of gay people. Some of them even happen to be in positions or have demeanours that might make them come across as antagonistic to just about anybody. It would still be a bit of a bad look to include a villain following the archetype in which their queer coding (if not an overt sexual orientation) is presented in terms that are directly threatening or loathsome. This is in spite of the fact that there do exist gay people who are predatory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T20:32:02-07:00","id":1296880,"title":"","content":"I do tend to hold wildly different views than many folks here, but I will ask regardless. Wouldn't indulging ideas like this be counterproductive? Wouldn't normalizing a given identity mean demonstrating they should be equally capable of villainy or heroism and everything between including everyday human flaws, emotions, or even pettiness?<br /> <br /> However, I suppose if there were a bit more to this specific story than window dressing to the trope it wouldn't leave such an ashen taste. Alas, it doesn't seem word count would permit the gravity her story would require to hit a more interesting note without just doing something completely different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13326-aredin","name":"Aredin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T21:17:37-07:00","id":1296898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296530#post1296530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with this but I do think the relationship being an issue near the end was an important detail. Also, she's no longer &quot;one of the best martial artists in creation&quot; anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>She's still a &quot;legendary martial artist&quot; by the standards of the Silver Pact / First Age, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T21:26:12-07:00","id":1296900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296898#post1296898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She's still a &amp;quot;legendary martial artist&amp;quot; by the standards of the Silver Pact / First Age, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>But she only has white reaper. Someone like her should have multiple styled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T22:12:24-07:00","id":1296909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296900#post1296900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But she only has white reaper. Someone like her should have multiple styled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T22:50:17-07:00","id":1296912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296900#post1296900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But she only has white reaper. Someone like her should have multiple styled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars can combo martial arts and their natural charms so they don't have as much incentive to go multi-style to try and plug up the holes in their first style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T22:54:20-07:00","id":1296913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aredin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296880#post1296880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't normalizing a given identity mean demonstrating they should be equally capable of villainy or heroism and everything between including everyday human flaws, emotions, or even pettiness?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The trick is to not recall archetypes that have been alternately used to create an image that perpetuates marginalization and oppression, or appropriating and broadening traits to use them as a shorthand for something negative, such as deviance and villainy in the case of the queer-coded antagonist. <br /> <br /> Although even that has intersections that complicate it, given how there have been coded villains that have been adopted by LGBT people and subcultures for a number of reasons.<br /> <br /> And there's a whole thing about the basis of shorthand in narrative construction and general psychology, which is too much to get into here, but can be basically summarized with &quot;be careful with the images you put forward, because your medium is always going to simplify it, and the audience is going to use shortcuts to internalise it&quot;.<br /> <br /> I just want to briefly draw attention to the fact that the extent of my proposed responses to something would be rolling eyes and calling it a bad look; I think as reactions go, those are fairly benign. The point isn't to write something off, or even say never use it again at all (at least for these subjects, there are definitely things I don't think should be in media in general and these books in particular again, but they're more extreme), just to be mindful of where they come from and how they might influence.<br /> <br /> To borrow a phrase from somebody whom I greatly respect, the point isn't to say &quot;thing bad&quot;, just that thing exists.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T23:01:18-07:00","id":1296914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296912#post1296912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lunars can combo martial arts and their natural charms so they don't have as much incentive to go multi-style to try and plug up the holes in their first style.</div> </div> </div> </div>More importantly, I think we can presume that Lilith's reputation would be based primarily on her having gone out and used her martial arts to actually accomplish things. I think that should be a more important basis for measuring Exalted, and any other characters, than how many things they can do theoretically.<br /> <br /> Plus, the chapter went and gave us a damn introduction pointing out that the write-ups cannot possibly be comprehensive and should be filled out according to gameplay needs and how one envisions the character. Lilith has White Reaper Style because it has always been her signature; if one can only envision her martial arts prowess, one of her key features, in terms of knowing more Styles, then just give them to her.<br /> <br /> Besides, what was it Bruce Lee said about the difference between practicing one kick ten thousand times, and ten thousand kicks once?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T23:23:25-07:00","id":1296918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296914#post1296914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More importantly, I think we can presume that Lilith's reputation would be based primarily on her having gone out and used her martial arts to actually accomplish things. I think that should be a more important basis for measuring Exalted, and any other characters, than how many things they can do theoretically.<br /> <br /> Plus, the chapter went and gave us a damn introduction pointing out that the write-ups cannot possibly be comprehensive and should be filled out according to gameplay needs and how one envisions the character. Lilith has White Reaper Style because it has always been her signature; if one can only envision her martial arts prowess, one of her key features, in terms of knowing more Styles, then just give them to her.<br /> <br /> Besides, what was it Bruce Lee said about the difference between practicing one kick ten thousand times, and ten thousand kicks once?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd throw in my two cents on top of this.<br /> <br /> We think alot in terms of rules, but 'Legendary' and 'the best' are not usually terms that get thrown around at people that dally back and forth between a thousand things. Each Martial Art is its own animal and just because players like to see how many they can cram into a single character does not mean it is realistic or even really good storytelling. Heck, Exalted even incorporates alot of very distinct visuals and aesthetics to specific martial arts which make them even more different than formalized combat styles already are irl (to say nothing of the fact that they tend to do wildly different things).<br /> <br /> Having a <i>character </i>which the ST is supposed to describe and use would be a nightmare for me if their design was as busy as giving four completely different styles would be.<br /> <br /> Lilith is a really old Lunar who has a channeled her essence into perfecting a Martial Art designed to literally kill entire armies, isn't that sort of 'legendary' on its own?<br /> <br /> Beyond the land of Min-Maxed-Villain(Which you probably shouldnt use)-polis, few Exalts achieve such heights as to be able to master the essence of an MA, fewer would <i>be </i>martial artists and who knows how many of that incredibly small specific group are masters of the White Reaper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 03-15-2019, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T00:12:41-07:00","id":1296927,"title":"","content":"Superficial thought, but with the new backstory do you think she'll have a different appearence too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T04:45:46-07:00","id":1296942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aredin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296880#post1296880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't indulging ideas like this be counterproductive? Wouldn't normalizing a given identity mean demonstrating they should be equally capable of villainy or heroism and everything between including everyday human flaws, emotions, or even pettiness?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely, and if all goes well we\u2019ll actually reach that point some day. In the meantime though, evening out the number of \u201cgood\u201d vs. \u201cbad\u201d portrayals of a class of people goes a lot faster if you come at it from both directions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T05:00:33-07:00","id":1296947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296692#post1296692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, for the Dragonblooded the usurpation happened like 1400 years ago, that\u2019s like 24 dragon blooded generations ago (given their extended lifespan) that\u2019s like saying people in America don\u2019t study Columbus\u2019s arrival because it\u2019s ancient history.</div> </div> </div> </div> How accurate is your typical American's knowledge of Columbus though?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just think that it seems a bit silly, givent that the terrestrial book is filled with stories about how terrestrials and the realm are corrupt/mismanaging things, they didn\u2019t bother including examples of celestial behavior that could even be pointed at by an extremist to legitimize their treatment of solars as anathema.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think establishing Facts does the job just fine. They're not going to be complicated stories and basically consist of Celestials doing *horrible thing* for no discernible reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T05:08:17-07:00","id":1296949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296947#post1296947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> How accurate is your typical American's knowledge of Columbus though?<br /> <br /> I think establishing Facts does the job just fine. They're not going to be complicated stories and basically consist of Celestials doing *horrible thing* for no discernible reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) I\u2019m actually not talking about accuracy merely that the subject comes up with some detail\u2014 I wouldn\u2019t anticipate the Realm accurately report a nuanced view of solar rule, only of the atrocity of it. But what they actually spread is a fictionalized version of history that has no basis in fact (at least at the outset they would have KNOWN the solars weren\u2019t possessed) so while the fiction serves as a useful tool to manipulate the populace it doesn\u2019t seem like it would be useful or taken seriously (especially initially) by scholars amongst the dragonblooded.<br /> 2) why not? we are very aware of stories of famous leaders doing horrible things for no decernable reason (caligula killing giraffes in the arena, Nero playing the violin, Rasputin and his sex parties, Vlad Tepes and his commitment to making sure his enemeies were properly skewered, Romans in general and their love of crucificition, nazi war horrors of various stripes etc) the Facts are driven home by the annecdotes. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s not my intent to argue and I appreciate that others don\u2019t agree and I\u2019m fine with that. I don\u2019t think they are wrong (it\u2019s all a fiction anyway) I was just sharing my feelings and thoughts on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T05:09:14-07:00","id":1296950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296927#post1296927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Superficial thought, but with the new backstory do you think she'll have a different appearence too?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well she\u2019s dark skinned now. So that\u2019s kinda new\u2014 iirc she was very fair in the past","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T05:27:45-07:00","id":1296953,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I mean 'Facts' as in players being able to use the Lore ability to introduce information and that such anecdotes are pretty easy to come up with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T07:23:48-07:00","id":1296976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296753#post1296753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the Realm era, the majority of Dragon Blooded barely live to a hundred. I presume that might go double for the extreme violence of the Shogunate.<br /> <br /> Practically speaking, the longevity of the Terrestrial Exalted comes out less as them having fewer generations, and more as them having generations of regular length in which almost everybody stays pretty until misadventure, intrigue or war takes them, and at big family gatherings there'll be a few venerable fossils who'll command a lot of attention, but probably be too busy or important for you to talk to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also generally always a cohort of 20-40 year olds who when they come into power also start defining things. Like, just becuase my granddad is sitll alive today, while it was less likely a hudnred years ago, doesn't mean I suddenly ahve this huge bit of personal cultural experience and knowledge with the 1940s and 1950s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T07:36:36-07:00","id":1296983,"title":"","content":"To kind of expand. Remember that the Civil Rights Era was <i>50</i> years and there's already a lot of whitewashing and misremembering and mischarecterization of a lot of it. The Berlin Wall came down only 30 years ago, and yet there's a pretty notable chunk of folks who were alive hten that there bieng mroe than one Germany is just not a thing. Shit changes so much in <i>one</i> generation. And things do kind of shift around every couple decades for a lot of socieites. Having a 200 year old grandpa doesn't change the views of a Dragon-Blood who's only 20 that 200 years ago is just out of her experience. Shit, she probably doens't even conceptualize Iselsi as a house, even if its denotion was in her lifetime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T07:55:14-07:00","id":1296990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296983#post1296983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To kind of expand. Remember that the Civil Rights Era was <i>50</i> years and there's already a lot of whitewashing and misremembering and mischarecterization of a lot of it. The Berlin Wall came down only 30 years ago, and yet there's a pretty notable chunk of folks who were alive hten that there bieng mroe than one Germany is just not a thing. Shit changes so much in <i>one</i> generation. And things do kind of shift around every couple decades for a lot of socieites. Having a 200 year old grandpa doesn't change the views of a Dragon-Blood who's only 20 that 200 years ago is just out of her experience. Shit, she probably doens't even conceptualize Iselsi as a house, even if its denotion was in her lifetime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun example, look at our own last five generations and how each conceptualized the events of the last century. Its very hard to find anywhere on the planet in my experience that where you arent going to find massive perception gaps about wars, cultural movements and political upheavels between generations that are all still alive. Despite it heing the equivalent of two minutes in historical terms.<br /> <br /> Heck, how much revisionism does the average person go through in their own life as memory fades or mixes with new opinions and thoughts? <br /> <br /> There is also no such thing as a writer without a bias, we try very hard (in academic works, and even then sometimes) to be clear today about them today but that is a bit of an anomoly in the grand scheme of things. For most of human history people have tended to put down what was convenient and change details that did not suit them as a matter of course. Now it is very easy to judge this as amoral but you have to remember that the perception was usually different than ours. You were typically writing to communicate some lesson drawn from the past, how accurate said events were tended to be pretty secondary and we still struggle not to demonize political and ideological opponents today.<br /> <br /> Put another way, telling the Realm to write perfectly accurate and unbiased history is very much throwing orichalcum rocks when we live in glass houses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T08:22:06-07:00","id":1296992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296990#post1296990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun example, look at our own last five generations and how each conceptualized the events of the last century. Its very hard to find anywhere on the planet in my experience that where you arent going to find massive perception gaps about wars, cultural movements and political upheavels between generations that are all still alive. Despite it heing the equivalent of two minutes in historical terms.<br /> <br /> Heck, how much revisionism does the average person go through in their own life as memory fades or mixes with new opinions and thoughts? <br /> <br /> There is also no such thing as a writer without a bias, we try very hard (in academic works, and even then sometimes) to be clear today about them today but that is a bit of an anomoly in the grand scheme of things. For most of human history people have tended to put down what was convenient and change details that did not suit them as a matter of course. Now it is very easy to judge this as amoral but you have to remember that the perception was usually different than ours. You were typically writing to communicate some lesson drawn from the past, how accurate said events were tended to be pretty secondary and we still struggle not to demonize political and ideological opponents today.<br /> <br /> Put another way, telling the Realm to write perfectly accurate and unbiased history is very much throwing orichalcum rocks when we live in glass houses.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point that\u2019s being missed Here, or rather the point that is being argued, is actually tangential to my argument. I\u2019m not saying they should have an accurate or necessarily fair view of history, I fully expect it to be distorted, but they don\u2019t appear to really engage with it in a realistic way\u2014 anathema are bad because theyre demons and maybe they ran the world at some point, then the dragons rose up and fixed that. Sure great, but where are the stories or terrestrial heroism in the face of anathema oppression, where are the equivalents of King David or other biblical heroes, where are the accounts of specifically heinous tyrants. (beyond the 5 immaculate dragons, which, to be fair, is a really not very many) it\u2019s not that I think they should have a fair or impartial view or history, that\u2019s actually kind of the opposite, but that it would have been politically useful to engage with it more (much they way the Bible did) and its curious that in the setting they dont appear to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T08:44:01-07:00","id":1296997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296992#post1296992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point that\u2019s being missed Here, or rather the point that is being argued, is actually tangential to my argument. I\u2019m not saying they should have an accurate or necessarily fair view of history, I fully expect it to be distorted, but they don\u2019t appear to really engage with it in a realistic way\u2014 anathema are bad because theyre demons and maybe they ran the world at some point, then the dragons rose up and fixed that. Sure great, but where are the stories or terrestrial heroism in the face of anathema oppression, where are the equivalents of King David or other biblical heroes, where are the accounts of specifically heinous tyrants. (beyond the 5 immaculate dragons, which, to be fair, is a really not very many) it\u2019s not that I think they should have a fair or impartial view or history, that\u2019s actually kind of the opposite, but that it would have been politically useful to engage with it more (much they way the Bible did) and its curious that in the setting they dont appear to.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not an unfair view, but I think you might want to take a less moderm view on it. We have spent the few centuries trying very hard to de-mythologize alot of world history, but the fact of the matter is that those sort of grand myths and legends overlapping major events was not that uncommon.<br /> <br /> One of my favorite examples of this is medieval culture and Alexandria. Sure, if you asked a scholar they could have given you some very rough details on the city's founding (Egypt has long been a seat of learning), but most people would have told you the common stories. How Alexander went underwater in a magical glass ball to survey the grounds and scarred off sea monsters with his sheer awesomeness. <br /> <br /> Japanese court histories were decent but in local conception, one area where a major battle against a group believed to be related to the Ainu (cant recall the name atm) was long understood as site of a war against an army of literal demons.<br /> <br /> You can really find examples of these sort of things anywhere, why should you not in Creation? Especially when this is a place where worrying about hordes of ghosts, demons and angry gods trying to destory everything is not just believable, it is much more understandable to most people than the Usurpation. <br /> <br /> Hell, there are probably plenty of places where &quot;And on the eighth day the great sorcerer so spoke, &quot;Dude, my house should have chicken legs&quot;, and so it was made&quot; is a 100% accurate recollection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T09:40:44-07:00","id":1297007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296992#post1296992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point that\u2019s being missed Here, or rather the point that is being argued, is actually tangential to my argument. I\u2019m not saying they should have an accurate or necessarily fair view of history, I fully expect it to be distorted, but they don\u2019t appear to really engage with it in a realistic way\u2014 anathema are bad because theyre demons and maybe they ran the world at some point, then the dragons rose up and fixed that. Sure great, but where are the stories or terrestrial heroism in the face of anathema oppression, where are the equivalents of King David or other biblical heroes, where are the accounts of specifically heinous tyrants. (beyond the 5 immaculate dragons, which, to be fair, is a really not very many) it\u2019s not that I think they should have a fair or impartial view or history, that\u2019s actually kind of the opposite, but that it would have been politically useful to engage with it more (much they way the Bible did) and its curious that in the setting they dont appear to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some actual interaction with the Immaculate texts would be great given how important they are to the lives of a lot of Dragon-Blooded characters.<br /> <br /> To show you where I'm coming from this is an example of the kind of content which I think is superfluous as actual 100% canon, propaganda free, objective observer, final destination! setting fact.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Compass Blessed Isle page 10</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On one Solar estate, half of the thousands of mortal servants were given roots and bark-like skin and planted in elaborate gardens. In another mansion, hundreds of mortals were altered so that their screams became inhumanly lovely and melodious. The Exalt who owned this mansion crafted beautiful, merciless automata to play upon the flesh of these servants, and powerful life-preserving Charms and artifacts kept the servants alive. The Exalt put on performances that lasted for many days at a time and were renowned for both the beauty of the music and the inventiveness and extremity of the tortures used.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T09:48:08-07:00","id":1297010,"title":"","content":"<i>The Realm</i>'s section on the Immaculate Text and the role the Immaculate Order plays in recording and promulgating history directly addresses a lot of the stuff being raised here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T09:51:35-07:00","id":1297012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297007#post1297007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some actual interaction with the Immaculate texts would be great given how important they are to the lives of a lot of Dragon-Blooded characters.<br /> <br /> To show you where I'm coming from this is an example of the kind of content which I think is superfluous as actual 100% canon, propaganda free, objective observer, final destination! setting fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then Dreams made it 100% canon though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T10:08:26-07:00","id":1297015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296950#post1296950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well she\u2019s dark skinned now. So that\u2019s kinda new\u2014 iirc she was very fair in the past</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, as far as I know, the only picture of Lilith that is in colour is on the cover of Manual: Lunars, and I'd say she's at least olive-skinned on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T10:12:04-07:00","id":1297016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296992#post1296992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point that\u2019s being missed Here, or rather the point that is being argued, is actually tangential to my argument. I\u2019m not saying they should have an accurate or necessarily fair view of history, I fully expect it to be distorted, but they don\u2019t appear to really engage with it in a realistic way\u2014 anathema are bad because theyre demons and maybe they ran the world at some point, then the dragons rose up and fixed that. Sure great, but where are the stories or terrestrial heroism in the face of anathema oppression, where are the equivalents of King David or other biblical heroes, where are the accounts of specifically heinous tyrants. (beyond the 5 immaculate dragons, which, to be fair, is a really not very many) it\u2019s not that I think they should have a fair or impartial view or history, that\u2019s actually kind of the opposite, but that it would have been politically useful to engage with it more (much they way the Bible did) and its curious that in the setting they dont appear to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite a few were in the Aspect books.<br /> <br /> Which is not me saying that you're wrong, rather that we need some medium that would allow for the presence of the kind of stuff that was in the Aspect books. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T10:32:40-07:00","id":1297022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297015#post1297015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, as far as I know, the only picture of Lilith that is in colour is on the cover of Manual: Lunars, and I'd say she's at least olive-skinned on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>she was also in a bunch of the comics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T10:48:20-07:00","id":1297025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297022#post1297022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">she was also in a bunch of the comics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which ones?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T10:51:36-07:00","id":1297026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297025#post1297025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>There was one in sidereals where she fights what's her face. There was also one using the same design in dreams but both were based on the 1e look if I remember correctly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T10:54:41-07:00","id":1297029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297026#post1297026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was one in sidereals where she fights what's her face. There was also one using the same design in dreams but both were based on the 1e look if I remember correctly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sooo\u2026 pictures that were <b>not</b> in colour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T12:26:31-07:00","id":1297058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297029#post1297029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sooo\u2026 pictures that were <b>not</b> in colour.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think your right, her description says \u201cdark skinned\u201d in fangs at the gates as I recall though which I take to mean darker than tan or olive skin. But that could just be me\u2014 I tend to picture dark skinned as being PANTONE 2431 C or darker in complexion. Big chunk of my family is Syrian so my threshold for dark might be higher than normal though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T12:29:11-07:00","id":1297059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296582#post1296582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> People never moving on happens pretty often in fiction, most characters just don't have the opportunity to spend centuries not moving on (but conversely they also can't usually say the relationship they are mourning <i>lasted</i> centuries either). And usually their not moving on also involves them dealing with it in an amazingly unhealthy way on top of never finishing the dealing with of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is pretty common in general, however is probably filtered through particularly tendency of heroic fiction to have active protagonists and antagonists who tend to skew male, such that even male characters who &quot;don't move on&quot; end up more like Rakan Thulio (a non-stalker-ish version of Rakan Thulio at least), rather than not doing anything. Even in heroic fiction you have plenty of male characters who go off and lose their wife or something and just dwell on in forever, but they're usually explicitly &quot;Old Farmer X&quot;, &quot;Censor who did nothing when they killed his wife, until protagonist man turns up&quot; and such.<br /> <br /> Probably at least somewhat less pronounced in literary fiction where it's more about reactions and internal psychology rather than active -agonists doing deeds, and much of the time there's little plot being driven forward by actions at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T12:47:20-07:00","id":1297060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297012#post1297012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then Dreams made it 100% canon though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was already canon. However, as time has gone on I've come to question the benefit of that beyond its utility to people arguing over the internet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T12:57:39-07:00","id":1297062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297059#post1297059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is pretty common in general, however is probably filtered through particularly tendency of heroic fiction to have active protagonists and antagonists who tend to skew male, such that even male characters who &amp;quot;don't move on&amp;quot; end up more like Rakan Thulio (a non-stalker-ish version of Rakan Thulio at least), rather than not doing anything. Even in heroic fiction you have plenty of male characters who go off and lose their wife or something and just dwell on in forever, but they're usually explicitly &amp;quot;Old Farmer X&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Censor who did nothing when they killed his wife, until protagonist man turns up&amp;quot; and such.<br /> <br /> Probably at least somewhat less pronounced in literary fiction where it's more about reactions and internal psychology rather than active -agonists doing deeds, and much of the time there's little plot being driven forward by actions at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference here though is unlike leviathan and mahasuchi she didn\u2019t just bow out and do her own thing, she took on the mind of an owl to avoid her emotional pain entering what, If she weren\u2019t an Exalt, would amount to a centuries long fugue state\u2014 the Reaction to trauma with mental illness of some sort is a trope that overwhelmingly skews female in literature except where mental illness is the subject of the peice in general. Consider Lady Macbeth, who went totally nutso well before her husband became an anti forest paranoiac. I feel like again I should clarify I\u2019m not hating on the character or the work and I only keep engaging because I feel like my initial point is getting slightly misunderstood. It\u2019s not just madness or just passivity it\u2019s the combination of both that I kind of feel a bit \u201cmeh\u201d about","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T13:06:34-07:00","id":1297063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297060#post1297060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was already canon. However, as time has gone on I've come to question the benefit of that beyond its utility to people arguing over the internet.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was useful because while over the top it presented how mad the solars went. I do prefer an objective view of the usurpation because otherwise it just seems like solars could do no wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T13:21:36-07:00","id":1297068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297058#post1297058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think your right, her description says \u201cdark skinned\u201d in fangs at the gates as I recall though which I take to mean darker than tan or olive skin. But that could just be me\u2014 I tend to picture dark skinned as being PANTONE 2431 C or darker in complexion. Big chunk of my family is Syrian so my threshold for dark might be higher than normal though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I know, I'm just thinking that it might not be as much of a departure as it first appears.<br /> <br /> She's described as having been born in the South, which I'm not sure if she ever was before... yes, although it required plumbing the depths of her write-up in Lords of Creation (eeuurgh), in Second Edition she was referred to as Northeastern, compared to now having been born in an enclave of the desert. Presumably when we get art, she'll be more distinctly dark-skinned (even if brown skin is still an Eastern feature).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297059#post1297059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even in heroic fiction you have plenty of male characters who go off and lose their wife or something and just dwell on in forever, but they're usually explicitly &quot;Old Farmer X&quot;, &quot;Censor who did nothing when they killed his wife, until protagonist man turns up&quot; and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that's right.<br /> <br /> The problem I have tended to find is a difference in framing in which a woman character with such an experience feels like they're being portrayed as characteristically fragile, while men characters have a persistent issue with women in their lives being used as props for their tragedy, and to motivate them into righteous vengeance.<br /> <br /> It's not in every single instance of either, but there are patterns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T13:37:40-07:00","id":1297070,"title":"","content":"I think it's very hard to know what's wrong or right here; I'm only offering a perspective and subjective experience here. It's essentially not going to be possible to prove that some trope is disproportionately popular or anything, or that when women are portrayed as passive or at risk of sanity following rupture of a relationship it's &quot;different&quot; than for men (in these sort of arguments, I find participants will just be selective to the ends supporting their argument, until it becomes totally untenable, unlike other arguments where persuasion is actually totally possible and changing minds is possible). <br /> <br /> To be frank, these discussions often generally become unproductive and end up with people simply hardening their position to reflect their broader gender political beliefs (particularly since it has become common to try and argue that media causes culture, a position that has become more popular since the heyday of arguments that people are free to watch and read whatever they want without needing censorship to protect their moral fibre, since words have no deep effect). So I will bow out now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T13:50:27-07:00","id":1297075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297070#post1297070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's essentially not going to be possible to prove that some trope is disproportionately popular or anything, or that when women are portrayed as passive or at risk of sanity following rupture of a relationship it's &quot;different&quot; than for men (in these sort of arguments, I find participants will just be selective to the ends supporting their argument, until it becomes totally untenable, unlike other arguments where persuasion is actually totally possible and changing minds is possible).</div> </div> </div> </div>The subject is not without attendant academia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be frank, these discussions often generally become unproductive and end up with people simply hardening their position to reflect their broader gender political beliefs</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but some people can be reflective enough to consider and reconsider their viewpoints; twelve years ago one would have found a very different Levi. And continuous circulation of the discourse is the only way the status quo is ever going to shift.<br /> <br /> Fangs at the Gate does not have consistent references to people across the gender spectrum because queer people silently waited their turn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(particularly since it has become common to try and argue that media causes culture, a position that has become more popular since the heyday of arguments that people are free to watch and read whatever they want without needing censorship to protect their moral fibre, since words have no deep effect).</div> </div> </div> </div>Social science is as capable of improving over time as any other field.<br /> <br /> Also, it's harder to argue that people have a moral fibre that is not susceptible to the rhetoric they're exposed to and the media that they consume in this current age of enormous harassment campaigns and a correlation between increasingly virulent screeds in response to growing diversity and a rise in the frequency of mass murders motivated by race, gender and sexual orientation.<br /> <br /> There is a substantive difference between the moral fibre that orthodox conservative authorities want to protect by curtailing alternative viewpoints and the one that traditionally marginalized people whose voices are becoming more prominent want to protect by challenging harmful narratives and the occasional straight-up Nazi.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T16:21:17-07:00","id":1297108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297059#post1297059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is pretty common in general, however is probably filtered through particularly tendency of heroic fiction to have active protagonists and antagonists who tend to skew male, such that even male characters who &quot;don't move on&quot; end up more like Rakan Thulio (a non-stalker-ish version of Rakan Thulio at least), rather than not doing anything. Even in heroic fiction you have plenty of male characters who go off and lose their wife or something and just dwell on in forever, but they're usually explicitly &quot;Old Farmer X&quot;, &quot;Censor who did nothing when they killed his wife, until protagonist man turns up&quot; and such.<br /> <br /> Probably at least somewhat less pronounced in literary fiction where it's more about reactions and internal psychology rather than active -agonists doing deeds, and much of the time there's little plot being driven forward by actions at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>For some reason I keep forgetting that Rakan Thulio started his shit over feeling entitled to the man he loved and getting pissy when the guy had the 'gall' to say he wasn't interested. And that he is so salty about it to this day that he took time out of his War on Heaven to let everyone know &quot;remember guys, one of the solars coming back is the reincarnation of the sword priest so if you want a notch on your belt giving credibility to the claim of being the best sword user alive kick his shit in! And as a bonus you might get the power to auto-unlock artifact evocations!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T21:56:58-07:00","id":1297154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297075#post1297075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it's harder to argue that people have a moral fibre that is not susceptible to the rhetoric they're exposed to and the media that they consume in this current age of enormous harassment campaigns and a correlation between increasingly virulent screeds in response to growing diversity and a rise in the frequency of mass murders motivated by race, gender and sexual orientation.<br /> <br /> There is a substantive difference between the moral fibre that orthodox conservative authorities want to protect by curtailing alternative viewpoints and the one that traditionally marginalized people whose voices are becoming more prominent want to protect by challenging harmful narratives and the occasional straight-up Nazi.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems that the content of your second argument clearly seems to prove your first here, I think the fact that this is where the conversation led to, proves Ghosthead's about being generally non-productive. So I too will bow out here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13326-aredin","name":"Aredin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T23:05:17-07:00","id":1297163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297108#post1297108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For some reason I keep forgetting that Rakan Thulio started his shit over feeling entitled to the man he loved and getting pissy when the guy had the 'gall' to say he wasn't interested. And that he is so salty about it to this day that he took time out of his War on Heaven to let everyone know &quot;remember guys, one of the solars coming back is the reincarnation of the sword priest so if you want a notch on your belt giving credibility to the claim of being the best sword user alive kick his shit in! And as a bonus you might get the power to auto-unlock artifact evocations!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I kind of wonder how many of the Get ,or other Exalts, upon finding out what started all that just end up dumbstruck for the next five minutes before going, &quot;Really?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T23:16:02-07:00","id":1297164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aredin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297154#post1297154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems that the content of your second argument clearly seems to prove your first here</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't <i>think</i> this is one of those occasions in which I find myself arguing with my own stated opinion earlier in the post, soooo... good?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aredin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the fact that this is where the conversation led to, proves Ghosthead's about being generally non-productive.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, at least one thing that they can produce is a sense of solidarity. Also adjusting the conversation away from the idea that thoughtful discussion of a subject's flaws, or even of the problematic connotations of a well-executed thing, is possible without anybody needing to feel as though they're being attacked. <br /> <br /> \u2026Ohhh dear, your point above was to imply that I'm somebody who has been conditioned by an ideology, and that my response to Ghosthead constitutes harassment, wasn't it? That's a bummer.<br /> <br /> Sure, bringing up the fact that Nazis are a thing that exists is a bit severe in this conversation about a particular character that is not one, but then, so is making a tacit inference that finding issues with something reminiscent of harmful stereotypes about how women cope with loss is akin to censorship driven by conservative moralising.<br /> <br /> Still, I suppose I could have found a more artful way to make the point that conservative authorities being censors was not bad because nobody is actually influenced by the art they consume anyway, it's bad because a lot of the kind of art that they would censor are things people <i>should</i> be influenced by (when it isn't so much theatre directed at scapegoats to make themselves feel big).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T23:20:28-07:00","id":1297165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297163#post1297163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I kind of wonder how many of the Get ,or other Exalts, upon finding out what started all that just end up dumbstruck for the next five minutes before going, &quot;Really?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not the ones who became Getimians after waking up one day and finding that their spouse and children no longer loved (and possibly remembered) them as a result of the designs of Heaven.<br /> <br /> It is amazing to me how often the motivation ascribed to Rakan Thulio is referred to with varying levels of contempt after the years I've had to listen to people complaining about Shun the Smiling Lady.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T00:10:48-07:00","id":1297171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297165#post1297165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably not the ones who became Getimians after waking up one day and finding that their spouse and children no longer loved (and possibly remembered) them as a result of the designs of Heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div>Debatable. I mean for one Rakan did also have the object of his affections killed, which would probably lose him a lot of sympathy from those that might have similar situations. Even the ones more directly responsible for those death's probably wouldn't be too kindly on it considering Rakan went and bound a hit into Fate, so future incarnations of his love would get killed. Plus the ones you're proposing would have actually lost loved ones, not just been denied due to the object of said affections not being into them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297165#post1297165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is amazing to me how often the motivation ascribed to Rakan Thulio is referred to with varying levels of contempt after the years I've had to listen to people complaining about Shun the Smiling Lady.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I have no idea who this Shun person is, so can't help you there. As for Rakan, well its an old thing. People tend to view things as needing a matching scale.* So with Rakan, we have a guy who has been, more or less, dutifully serving as one of the handymen of Fate since the Primordials fell. Then he goes and learns dark and forbidden secrets, declares war on Yu-Shan, digs up a long forgotten and sealed away (for gods only know what reason) type of Exalt to release upon the world, leads the new bearers of these powers in a war against the very Gods of this world and Destiny itself. All of this because at some point he was told &quot;He's just not into you dude.&quot; Oh it works, and it makes sense, its just bloody hilarious.<br /> <br /> <br /> *See countless incidents in movies, television, and such where a character's proffession has some life altering eye opening thing to it or is tied to some great person in their life as opposed to just being a thing the person enjoyed and was happy to find out they could make a living doing. Plus conspiracy theories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T00:31:20-07:00","id":1297177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297171#post1297171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Debatable. I mean for one Rakan did also have the object of his affections killed, which would probably lose him a lot of sympathy from those that might have similar situations. Even the ones more directly responsible for those death's probably wouldn't be too kindly on it considering Rakan went and bound a hit into Fate, so future incarnations of his love would get killed. Plus the ones you're proposing would have actually lost loved ones, not just been denied due to the object of said affections not being into them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I'm not really sure how much the comic's backstory is going to inform his ultimate portrayal, the story told about the Usurpation there is coming from an unreliable source, and the Sidereals were killing all of the Solars anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I have no idea who this Shun person is, so can't help you there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this a joke, or are you actually unaware of the Sidereal Charm of that name, in which &quot;shun&quot; is a verb, not a person's name?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Rakan, well its an old thing. People tend to view things as needing a matching scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what's an even older thing? Gods taking sides in really messy wars based on whether or not they lost a beauty pageant. Something even older than that is a great hero king challenging the powers of the Earth and trying to discover the secret of immortality, because he's unhappy that his bro died.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">See countless incidents in movies, television, and such where a character's proffession has some life altering eye opening thing to it or is tied to some great person in their life as opposed to just being a thing the person enjoyed and was happy to find out they could make a living doing. Plus conspiracy theories.</div> </div> </div> </div>See the rest of them in which a person makes extremely profound decisions that change the course of history because of something to do with a friend, a loved one, or the manner in which they wanted to live.<br /> <br /> Darth Vader's final heroic act was not predicated on an epiphany about the magnitude of the institutional evil of the Galactic Empire.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T01:31:28-07:00","id":1297179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297177#post1297177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, I'm not really sure how much the comic's backstory is going to inform his ultimate portrayal, the story told about the Usurpation there is coming from an unreliable source, and the Sidereals were killing all of the Solars anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last I heard still cannon. So Rakan went and killed his infatuation for reasons entirely unrelated to the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297177#post1297177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this a joke, or are you actually unaware of the Sidereal Charm of that name, in which &quot;shun&quot; is a verb, not a person's name?</div> </div> </div> </div>Never heard of the charm. Besides this is Exalted Shun the Smiling Lady is not the weirdest thing I've heard someone named in this game. Especially if you take the naming conventions for Abyssals into account.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297177#post1297177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what's an even older thing? Gods taking sides in really messy wars based on whether or not they lost a beauty pageant. Something even older than that is a great hero king challenging the powers of the Earth and trying to discover the secret of immortality, because he's unhappy that his bro died.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're getting where I'm giving the explanation off wrong. I'm talking about mental phenomon normal to human psyche as an explantion for why you tend to see people responding with varying levels of incredulity to the thing that started Rakan's whole schtick being started due to not getting the boy.<br /> <br /> Also God's are not considered human, and are usually seen as the scale. IE cheesing off a god and getting your forces decimated is considered a reasonable cause. Also you are doing terrible on your mythological reference there. The Trojan War was an abducted bride thing caused by said incident with the apple, none of the goddesses chose their sides in the war based on the pick because there wasn't a war until Aphrodite fullfilled her end of the bargain and abducted the wife of a different ruler which brought a ton of alliances into play on getting her back. Plus the Greek gods had a tendency to swap sides at the drop of a hat in the Illiad.<br /> <br /> As for the Gilgamesh one, nah that's usually presented as not wanting to die brought on by being forced to confront the loss of Enkidu. Which is hardly an abnormally scaled response, especially considering the stuff Gilgamesh had a tendency to get up to before that point anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297177#post1297177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See the rest of them in which a person makes extremely profound decisions that change the course of history because of something to do with a friend, a loved one, or the manner in which they wanted to live.<br /> <br /> Darth Vader's final heroic act was not predicated on an epiphany about the magnitude of the institutional evil of the Galactic Empire.</div> </div> </div> </div>First again missing the point of my statement. Second a lot of those tend to include intervening steps. IE Luke buys droids, which contain a message, which drags him into a series of events that culminate in the fall of the Empire. Not Luke buys droids and as a result the Empire falls. It helps for people to be able to see the whole chain of events. Like the indication that Lilith left the world due to a feeling of disconnect from it all over the course of the fighting and hard memories that she didn't have to deal with while being an owl. We get more steps so we can see it working and such. Right now Rakan's thing seems to be got dumped, or turned down, realized Fate was unfair because he seems to believe he's owed his love interest and therefore war against the world.<br /> <br /> The Vader thing feels iffy to me, considering the whole bit of Luke sparing him when the Emporer was telling Luke to kill Vader followed by Vader listening to his son ask for help while the dude who'd just offered Vader's position at the cost of Vader's fresh corpse was lightning bolting his son to death. Just saying there's a case to be made there for Vader's action there being the result of realizing that he's probably been the bad guy and that he probably has not been part of an organization that is just doing the harsh but necessary things for the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 03-16-2019, 04:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T01:46:15-07:00","id":1297180,"title":"","content":"There is other stuff I want to respond to, but I'll save it for when I turn my laptop back on. For now, this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297179#post1297179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never heard of the charm. Besides this is Exalted Shun the Smiling Lady is not the weirdest thing I've heard someone named in this game. Especially if you take the naming conventions for Abyssals into account.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow that is super weird.<br /> <br /> Okay, so Shun the Smiling Lady is a really basic Socialize Charm. I think it might be how their Socialize tree started, so basically any Sidereal invested in that Ability could use it.<br /> <br /> If a Sidereal uses it on you, it basically makes people stop loving you. At all. For as long as the Sidereal maintained mote commitment.<br /> <br /> It had different mechanical expressions at different points, and the 2.5 version gave it engagement in the form of letting people spend Willpower to delay its effect, but the core idea remained consistent; Sidereals had the power to make people stop loving you.<br /> <br /> But nobody connects that to the idea that Rakan Thulio blames Heaven for losing his love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T08:27:13-07:00","id":1297258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297179#post1297179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Last I heard still cannon. So Rakan went and killed his infatuation for reasons entirely unrelated to the Usurpation.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Vance the comic is not canon:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1296431#post1296431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The events of the comic are non-canonical; players should be able to be Sublime Danger's Solar mate or learn that one of their past incarnations was Rakan Thulio's ex-lover.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2/page12\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2/page12\"> Ask the Devs v2 - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2/page12\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2/page12 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> It seems that, in my hubris, I've let the original Ask the Devs thread get a bit too long. If y'all wouldn't mind posting any new questions here. Thread rules </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T09:11:08-07:00","id":1297266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297258#post1297258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to Vance the comic is not canon:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2/page12\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2/page12\"> Ask the Devs v2 - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2/page12\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2/page12 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> It seems that, in my hubris, I've let the original Ask the Devs thread get a bit too long. If y'all wouldn't mind posting any new questions here. Thread rules </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, good to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T09:47:44-07:00","id":1297272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297180#post1297180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is other stuff I want to respond to, but I'll save it for when I turn my laptop back on. For now, this:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Wow that is super weird.<br /> <br /> Okay, so Shun the Smiling Lady is a really basic Socialize Charm. I think it might be how their Socialize tree started, so basically any Sidereal invested in that Ability could use it.<br /> <br /> If a Sidereal uses it on you, it basically makes people stop loving you. At all. For as long as the Sidereal maintained mote commitment.<br /> <br /> It had different mechanical expressions at different points, and the 2.5 version gave it engagement in the form of letting people spend Willpower to delay its effect, but the core idea remained consistent; Sidereals had the power to make people stop loving you.<br /> <br /> But nobody connects that to the idea that Rakan Thulio blames Heaven for losing his love.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, now that you mention it that does sound like the kind of thing Chejop might do to lure a powerful sidereal elder infatuated with a solar over to the 'lets kill all the solars' side. Wouldn't be the first time he did something that sounded like a good idea at the time but had serious consequences later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297258#post1297258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to Vance the comic is not canon:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2/page12\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2/page12\"> Ask the Devs v2 - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2/page12\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2/page12 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> It seems that, in my hubris, I've let the original Ask the Devs thread get a bit too long. If y'all wouldn't mind posting any new questions here. Thread rules </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>RIP Wandering FLare and that guy who looked exactly like Byakuya Kuchiki.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T09:48:50-07:00","id":1297273,"title":"","content":"Chapter fiction and comics are always considered noncanonical or deuterocanonical. They're usually congruent enough with canon that you can easily integrate their contents into your game, but the rest of the game line doesn't consider them canon (except for events directly referenced outside of fiction/comics).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T10:14:27-07:00","id":1297284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297180#post1297180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is other stuff I want to respond to, but I'll save it for when I turn my laptop back on. For now, this:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Wow that is super weird.<br /> <br /> Okay, so Shun the Smiling Lady is a really basic Socialize Charm. I think it might be how their Socialize tree started, so basically any Sidereal invested in that Ability could use it.<br /> <br /> If a Sidereal uses it on you, it basically makes people stop loving you. At all. For as long as the Sidereal maintained mote commitment.<br /> <br /> It had different mechanical expressions at different points, and the 2.5 version gave it engagement in the form of letting people spend Willpower to delay its effect, but the core idea remained consistent; Sidereals had the power to make people stop loving you.<br /> <br /> But nobody connects that to the idea that Rakan Thulio blames Heaven for losing his love.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one cared what it could do in general. People always hated what it did to their character and in 1e it was literally unblockable. You could stop the appearance effect but you couldn't stop everyone from no longer loving you. A lot of sidereals hatred comes from NPC sidereals who could do a lot of things in 1e which were unblockable but then again 1e was full of it on multiple levels it was just that sidereals had specific abilities to fuck people in ways lunars and solars didn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T10:37:16-07:00","id":1297289,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to figure out a way to describe the idea that maybe it's not that weird that people dislike the idea of a charm that has no resistances that basically ruins your life and the idea that the reason that the setting's new Ultra Cool Can't be Stopped Antagonist Who Everyone Hates Because He's Just So Cool is like that is that charm is not really contradictory.<br /> <br /> I don't think it is at all, but I'm not sure how to explain how it isn't. This isn't like sarcastic or anything, because it's a pretty odd series of circumstances, I guess is the best way to put it.<br /> <br /> But on some level I think it just shows the problem with Rakan Thulio isn't just 'he got mad because he didn't get his boyfriend'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":108,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","user":"Flare","date":". 03-16-2019, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T10:38:55-07:00","id":1297290,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it's harder to argue that people have a moral fibre that is not susceptible to the rhetoric they're exposed to and the media that they consume in this current age of enormous harassment campaigns and a correlation between increasingly virulent screeds in response to growing diversity and a rise in the frequency of mass murders motivated by race, gender and sexual orientation</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're talking about &quot;rhetoric&quot; (with the caveat &quot;and media&quot;) in a fairly widely sweeping manner here, while I'm talking (and this may not have been clear at all) about ideas around messaging that people are argued (with various degrees of plausibility) to receive through subtle tropes and images in narrative media culture.<br /> <br /> There's a difference between &quot;<i>People can respond to political rhetoric by changing ideas and attitudes about politics</i>&quot; which if they didn't, well, politics would be virtually impossible, and assertions that a particular subtle 'messages' in media received frequency of particular stories and character types are directly and strongly causal to a social attitude.<br /> <br /> It the difference between us saying &quot;<i>Watching shows about kung fu and drug taking every day makes you likely to go out and take drugs and punch someone in the face, and changes your fundamental attitudes about drug taking and violence towards more friendly ones</i>&quot; and &quot;<i>Telling people directly that they're being stolen from by the rich, in the harshest terms, will eventually tend to polarize their political opinion (in one direction or another)</i>&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you think there's a recent change in political culture, then look at the direct political messages moving around, and look deeper to the material drivers of conflict and polarization (economic and demographic change). If anything, our contemporary history is proof of the relative irrelevance of subtle cultural messaging in media consumption to political changes!<br /> <br /> (I want to stick to bowing out here so this the only bit I will respond to.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T12:58:55-07:00","id":1297332,"title":"","content":"Media is bad at affecting behaviour, but great at shaping world view.<br /> <br /> A person who consumes a lot of media about people doing drugs is highly unlikely to become a drug user just from that, and no other environmental factors. <br /> <br /> What it can do is shape what that person's view of the people who do drugs is. It will particularly reinforce a view instilled in them from other sources that they view as authoritative, or from their general upbringing.<br /> <br /> You consistently show people drug use as a moral failing rather than a medical issue, and associate it with a particular ethnicity, and that will have an effect on what they think of drug users.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T13:02:02-07:00","id":1297335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297284#post1297284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one cared what it could do in general. </div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe you didn't. I've seen other people of more sentiment who found the particulars extremely horrifying and objectionable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T13:17:46-07:00","id":1297342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297335#post1297335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe you didn't. I've seen other people of more sentiment who found the particulars extremely horrifying and objectionable.</div> </div> </div> </div>The power wasn't the issue though. No one had an issue with the power they only had an issue with the power used on them. Yeah it's rather horrifying that someone could just strike your name and make you hideous and fall out of love. However, the bitching was always about people using it on THEIR characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T13:38:08-07:00","id":1297344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297342#post1297342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The power wasn't the issue though. No one had an issue with the power they only had an issue with the power used on them. Yeah it's rather horrifying that someone could just strike your name and make you hideous and fall out of love. However, the bitching was always about people using it on THEIR characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I would expect that to have informed people's read on Raken Thulio blaming Heaven for his lost love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T13:54:13-07:00","id":1297349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297344#post1297344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I would expect that to have informed people's read on Raken Thulio blaming Heaven for his lost love.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe people would be more hopeful that Shun the Smiling Lady would become more interactive and present a way to have such a curse be more interesting as both a player and a PC rather then going 'well in 2E this makes sense'.<br /> <br /> After all, using a prior edition's mechanics (especially when the previous developers that made Rakan Thuilo spent a lot of time talking about how bad the previous edition was in regards to mechanics like that) to explain a new edition's villain is really weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T14:09:20-07:00","id":1297351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297344#post1297344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I would expect that to have informed people's read on Raken Thulio blaming Heaven for his lost love.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was pretty sure sidereals can't use it it on each other unless I'm misremembering. However, thulio's issue is that he blamed fate and heaven for it. However? Without definitive proof he's just a whiny asshole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T14:25:51-07:00","id":1297355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297349#post1297349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe people would be more hopeful that Shun the Smiling Lady would become more interactive and present a way to have such a curse be more interesting as both a player and a PC rather then going 'well in 2E this makes sense'.<br /> <br /> After all, using a prior edition's mechanics (especially when the previous developers that made Rakan Thuilo spent a lot of time talking about how bad the previous edition was in regards to mechanics like that) to explain a new edition's villain is really weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about mechanics, it's about how an iconic power of the Sidereals just happens to closely aligned with what a defector is accusing them of. Even if the specific Charm was not employed, it's still a thing that Sidereals do to people's relationships.<br /> <br /> All it takes to put them together is a bit of imagination and some reading in good faith.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297351#post1297351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was pretty sure sidereals can't use it it on each other unless I'm misremembering. However, thulio's issue is that he blamed fate and heaven for it. However? Without definitive proof he's just a whiny asshole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, you'll have melodramatic emotions in a pulp fantasy game inspired by ancient mythology.<br /> <br /> If all of the characters affected being compelled only by ultra logic and lacking in any kind of passion, they wouldn't be very engaging.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T14:30:18-07:00","id":1297356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297355#post1297355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not about mechanics, it's about how an iconic power of the Sidereals just happens to closely aligned with what a defector is accusing them of. Even if the specific Charm was not employed, it's still a thing that Sidereals do to people's relationships.<br /> <br /> All it takes to put them together is a bit of imagination and some reading in good faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if we do take your logic, he's still very 'I didn't care until it interfered with me, directly'<br /> <br /> EDIT: also excuse me for being confused but how did a topic about Lilith turn into one about Rakan Thulio.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T14:48:48-07:00","id":1297358,"title":"","content":"Since Lunars are good now maybe all threads will be Rakan thulio threads?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T14:54:40-07:00","id":1297359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297355#post1297355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, you'll have melodramatic emotions in a pulp fantasy game inspired by ancient mythology.<br /> <br /> If all of the characters affected being compelled only by ultra logic and lacking in any kind of passion, they wouldn't be very engaging.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that thulio acts like he was entitaled to someone. When the fact is that solars do whatever they want outside of yu-shan's designs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T15:17:12-07:00","id":1297367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297063#post1297063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was useful because while over the top it presented how mad the solars went. I do prefer an objective view of the usurpation because otherwise it just seems like solars could do no wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div> So you'd run a Gold Faction Sidereal game on the premise that the First Age Solars had torture parties like wine tasting events or would you downplay the fuck out of it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T15:34:53-07:00","id":1297371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297367#post1297367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So you'd run a Gold Faction Sidereal game on the premise that the First Age Solars had torture parties like wine tasting events or would you downplay the fuck out of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some solars might have done that, others might not have. The actions of a percentage of the population do not equate to the actions of the whole (I know you know that not trying to be condescending) I think the example\u2019s made in 2E are pretty trite and stupid but there does need to be some objective truly heinous (not just misunderstood but actually abominable viewed from a human perspective) occurences to drive something like the usurpation and it would help if there were some in setting examples. But yeah, I think you are right that some things are worse than nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T15:35:56-07:00","id":1297372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297367#post1297367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So you'd run a Gold Faction Sidereal game on the premise that the First Age Solars had torture parties like wine tasting events or would you downplay the fuck out of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>No one knows why the solars went crazy but it was evident that it wasn't explicitly every single one and the bad ones are counter argued by the good ones and the possibility of making them se the light.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T15:41:04-07:00","id":1297374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297356#post1297356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even if we do take your logic, he's still very 'I didn't care until it interfered with me, directly'<br /> <br /> EDIT: also excuse me for being confused but how did a topic about Lilith turn into one about Rakan Thulio.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm marking it down as a bit of pressure release since we have Lunars now and they're good. So that big worry is out of the way. Plus he's probably the thing we know the most about when discussing the Getimean owing to him being a Sidereal exalted and not one of the Getimean.<br /> <br /> Plus the bit of relief that comes from Lilith's story no longer being her as second fiddle and the insanely abused spouse of her mate because he decided to invent a mind rape suite of charms.<br /> I mean this incarnation feels more like something that PCs can interact with, you can empathize, criticize, ignore, or whatever regarding her eventual retreat from the world and her reasons for doing so. It's something approachable from an ST and PC perspective. I could be wrong, but I don't think I can really approach the old Desus backstory outside of a debate on whether or not killing the new incarnation is fair and maybe a debate on trying to get her to stop hunting said individual. Which doesn't feel as interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T15:48:29-07:00","id":1297376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297356#post1297356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even if we do take your logic, he's still very 'I didn't care until it interfered with me, directly'</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire republican movement of Ireland going mainstream was predicted on &quot;I didn't care until it affected me&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also a bunch of new Lunars, but that has less bite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297359#post1297359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is that thulio acts like he was entitaled to someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thulio acts like Heaven ran interference in a manner that was unjust.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the fact is that solars do whatever they want outside of yu-shan's designs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars are as susceptible to their Intimacies as anybody, and not all of them will have the Integrity Charms to protect their destinies from being shaped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T16:36:23-07:00","id":1297382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297376#post1297376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thulio acts like Heaven ran interference in a manner that was unjust.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Solars are as susceptible to their Intimacies as anybody, and not all of them will have the Integrity Charms to protect their destinies from being shaped.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which there is no proof that was the case and asva sidereal he'd have the means to work past that. He's bitter for what seems to be no reason other than pettiness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T17:43:32-07:00","id":1297400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297376#post1297376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thulio acts like Heaven ran interference in a manner that was unjust.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would care more if Thulio wasn't such a garbage character.<br /> <br /> This is a long ass post that I've had issues with for awhile, but basically Rakan Thulio is just a fucking worthless character and his existence in 3E makes the entire game less interesting and less good.<br /> <br /> I have never had a game that Rakan Thulio even tangentially appeared in that did not immediately implode, because Rakan Thulio is basically poison to any sort of game he's in due to how much ridiculous bullshit he is, all stacked on top of each other in this giant jenga pile of the worst aspects of 2E Deathlords, 2E Yozi, and 2E Sidereal Elders. Because the second a Getimien shows up, Rakan Thulio has to show up, and the second that Rakan Thulio shows up, the game has to be about him from then on.<br /> <br /> Rakan Thulio is toxic to the entire system of Exalted because of the way he works and who he is. He is a single person who we are repeatedly told is a big deal, and whenever there is a chance, they tell us how cool he is and what he's done. Rakan Thulio has an entire splat of Exalts at his beck and call, apparently almost perfectly to the point that one of the Getimen's key plot points is 'getting away from Rakan Thulio'. This is 2E Deathlords and non-fanon Yozi writ-large; a massively powerful being who can do whatever he wants to you and you are brainwashed into listening to him. It means any Getimien has to bring along Rakan Thulio no matter what, because he is their story. And when Rakan Thulio is in a game, he's the big bad guy now, because he's so smart, so intelligent, and so powerful that everyone else is basically just his toady. Even things that should, in theory, be cosmically powerful threats on their own end up feeling like lackys to this guy. He makes everyone else less important, because it turns out he does so much stuff or is implied to do so much stuff that is basically against the 'rules', and the implication is that this makes him cool.<br /> <br /> Rakan Thulio is not just a Sidereal, because that would be too 'boring' and not enough of a threat. He's a Sidereal that every major faction hates, but somehow can't deal with. He's an Original Sidereal Primordial War Survivor Sidereal Martial Artist Immortal, a great Hero who Everyone Loved who was visited by Saturn Herself and then who avoided Death through secret Martial Arts Techniques and became the World's Greatest Villain. And the game goes out of it's way to make sure it talks about him and how cool he is whenever it's possible. Every time the Getimiens come up, it's almost always, even just purely on word count, more about Rakan Thulio then the actual Exalt Type. It's like if the Lunars book was more about Luna and Gaia then the Lunars themselves, or an Abyssals book where it focused primarily on the Deathlords (oh wait...). Rakan Thulio gets a page spread in the Core Book. When Lunars talks about the strange Exalts that hate heaven as much as them, it turns out they don't. They instead reiterate about Rakan Thulio, who is so hated because he was an architect of the Usurpation. A third of the 100 word segment about the Getimiens is about Rakan Thulio. He is the worst part of Deathlords and Sidereals, because he feels like a guy whose sheet says 'I know every charm and every martial art, and I know where you are at all times'. What a boring thing to have in a game like this, which has been great so far in presenting that as just not being the case anymore; from Lunar Elders who aren't pathetically moping and doing nothing, to a Realm that is at once both terrifying and wracked with infighting and strife, but that if you aren't careful will team up to rip you to shreds before returning to fighting themselves. And then there's this guy, who feels like a relic of a time when the gameline was written to be about cosmically powered Beyond Exalts and Solars shooting up to Essence 7 to fist fight them while slaying thousands of Dragonblooded in a single sword swing and bouncing the Deathlords off the Elemental Poles to send them hurtling into Malfeas where they stay unable to move for 5 days. Rakan Thulio breaks the rules, but not just a rule in a dramatic way, he breaks all the rules, all together, in this giant pile of mush that stops being interesting because it stops coming across that Rakan Thulio is breaking rules in impressive ways, and more that just the rules don't apply to him and he can do whatever the fuck he wants; he's not an interesting NPC, he's the GM's pet whose the real protagonist, you're just there to watch him succeed, or when you are allowed to beat him there's a dramatic scene where you're supposed to feel very sad and he probably let you win anyway.<br /> <br /> The Getimians are a cool idea for a Splat, and people are clearly excited about them, and even I'm kinda excited about them and what they might be in how they are, but the idea that this entire splat type can't be used without this other guy is something that people yelled at in 2E. It's something that led to an entire Fanon that eventually swung back into Canon involving Infernals, where everyone would look at the stuff that told them how much control the Yozis had over them, then just go 'ROCKSTARS FROM HELL, ROCKSTARS FROM HELL, ROCKSTARS FROM HELL' and how 'well really, a Yozi has no power over you and they're basically just mentally disabled people with cosmic power. You can lie to them and say you'll help them then just never go to Malfeas, how can they stop you?' (it was important that you could lie to them, because in comparison, Abyssals could NEVER lie to the Deathlords, they always knew if you were faking), and eventually even the idea that they exalted from failures turned into 'well they could exalt just from not succeeding well enough, the failure isn't very important'. At the end, there were two competing feelings; of Infernals who could casually ignore the Yozi, or Infernals who, when they showed up, immediately demanded that the game turn into a game about The Yozi. And rather then acknowledge this as an issue when you have a splat so utterly defined by a patron like that, the decision was 'what if we just did that again, but this time made it an Exalt?'. And now it feels like details are so scarce on Getimians it's almost impossible to use them very effectively. In comparison, there's been so much information about Rakan Thulio that you can basically put him wherever. The Getimians don't feel like Exalts to me anymore, they feel like Rakan Thulio's Ork Lackies you're expected to cleave through on your way to him. And that's sad, because so many people are excited for them, and I want to like them, but I also have no desire to engage with Thulio.<br /> <br /> But it's not even entirely about Rakan Thulio and his presence in the game either, but also about the developers that put him there. Those people who railed against Neph for turning Infernals into an advertisement for his 'new game', who promised they were bringing big changes and were going to change Exalted, who were going to save the gameline, who really 'got it', because they played the game a lot and were just like us, who had swagger and confidence and everything. And then we watched them delay, and delay, and delay. And rant, and rave, and call things unfair, and insult and deride, and mock people. And then they release the first bit of Exalted media for 3E, before even the core, and we're introduced to their own spin on the Deathlords and the Yozi and the Elder Sidereals. He's what we see, and we're informed of just how important he is, through blog posts and forum posts and this book. And his important is further demanded; from the Style specifically made by his ex-lover, from the fact said ex-lover invented Evocations, from his page long spread in the core, from not being able to talk about Getimiens without Rakan Thulio, from a huge stretch goal being about another person embroiled in this cosmic love triangle in Sublime Danger, and HER unique Martial Arts Style Specifically For Her. All this stuff of dubious canonicity now, but it would be actively disingenuous to imply that because these are only 'secondarily-canon' that they do not change the perception of such things; the Scarlet Empress wasn't the Bride of the Ebon Dragon, until she was. These things do matter, regardless of the salve of 'it's not REALLY canon' put on it, and they change how people perceive things, especially when we were hungry for any kind of Exalted information at all. For all that they claimed that they were going to be different, in the end, all it meant was that they took all the overpowered NPCs and introduced an even bigger fish with their own stamp of 'this guy is the coolest and he is here to be cool, so make sure he's cool'. The same guys who now or used to spend time looking over previews of books written by our current developers and go 'oh yeah, I had a way better version of that written out, this version is trash, actually, but you'll never see it now!'<br /> <br /> Rakan Thulio's story might be appropriately 'epic' within the context of old legends. He might not be out of the ordinary of being a person spurned by love who is out for revenge against those who did it. He may even be right. I could tell you tons about Rakan Thulio and what he's done and his motivations, more then almost any other NPC (but not a thing about this other group of Exalts other then the one guy written up once in the Sidereal pre-booklet)<br /> <br /> But we live in a world where someone spouting those exact same beliefs sometimes picks up a gun and murders a dozen people, screaming about how 'The Government' should give them a girlfriend-slave who cooks for them, cleans for them, and fucks them whenever they want, because it's their rights. And you give me this asshole and you expect me to respect him, to like him, at all? You expect me to want him in the game, to engage with him legitimately? All the while the gameline goes out of it's way to yell 'look at how cool he is! Look at how cool! He's so cool!' about him and desperately present him as something that is just really going to bring the gameline together.<br /> <br /> No. I look at Rakan Thulio and I see the stuff that annoyed me about 2E Exalted- that annoyed so many people-, and I see the handiwork of a couple of guys who were never as good, as big, or as talented as they thought they were, and I see someone spouting beliefs that have murdered people in real life, and I see him being presented as something so cool that I should want to engage with him- even with him as a villain- and be happy when I am allowed to win against him.<br /> <br /> I will never ever appreciate that. That's why I get hung up with people defend Rakan Thulio, when they go 'His story is just based on Ancient Epics!', and all that other stuff. Because that's not the whole story, it's not the whole reason people dislike him, and it's just a very shallow observation on why a character might be disliked.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T17:51:17-07:00","id":1297402,"title":"","content":"Dude, the Getimians and Rakan Thulio have about three paragraphs to them in Exalted. You're seriously overstating everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T17:56:54-07:00","id":1297404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297402#post1297402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude, the Getimians and Rakan Thulio have about three paragraphs to them in Exalted. You're seriously overstating everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously. I know I have a penchant for exaggeration, myself, but you'd think Thulio's name was on every page of the book, with a rant like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T18:07:53-07:00","id":1297405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297400#post1297400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have never had a game that Rakan Thulio even tangentially appeared in that did not immediately implode, because Rakan Thulio is basically poison to any sort of game he's in due to how much ridiculous bullshit he is, all stacked on top of each other in this giant jenga pile of the worst aspects of 2E Deathlords, 2E Yozi, and 2E Sidereal Elders. Because the second a Getimien shows up, Rakan Thulio has to show up, and the second that Rakan Thulio shows up, the game has to be about him from then on.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've used him in games? Why?<br /> There's no rules for Getimians, they're mentioned in one paragraph as is he.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest, I didn't much like him, he looked like he might be a Gary-Sue, but I can't really form much of an opinion when he's just a preview of a book that's out in about 3 years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T18:25:15-07:00","id":1297408,"title":"","content":"Hmm... respond to one line, respond to incomprehensible ranting wall of text.<br /> <br /> {makes that hand gesture of weighing things up}<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297382#post1297382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which there is no proof that was the case</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I know that we're both imposing meanings on the text, but I'm imposing a meaning that actually accounts for the intended purpose of the character and their place in the setting that references long-standing and well known details about what the Sidereal Exalted actually do (many of which, even beyond that one Socialize Charm, have been a basis for complaints about the extent of their power and nature of their agendas <i>for years</i>*), and trying to imagine ways that they all fit together, with maybe a hint of suspension of disbelief to let the insignificant side inconsistencies slide if they're present, and you're imposing the meaning that would make the character terrible and the intent behind it dumb and wrong.<br /> <br /> To me, this is the very definition of the difference between reading in good and bad faith.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">asva sidereal he'd have the means to work past that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they appear to consist of having torn his thread from the Loom of Fate and denying Destiny's authority over his life and death.<br /> <br /> Like, that's the whole point; he's an antagonist. His actions and decisions are there to generate meaningful drama. So here we've got a character with a deep insight into the workings of Destiny who found that it had done him some kind of wrong, and thus came to some conclusion (currently uncertain as to precisely what) that caused him to reject the system outright, rather than dutifully submit to it.<br /> <br /> Much like, when the British responded to an uprising by rounding up any Irish person with even the vaguest hint of political affiliation with the rebels into concentration camps, and began executing leaders in a judicially dubious manner, the response of the Irish people was not &quot;well, it was our fault for making them mad; maybe if we make the right appeals to the proper channels, the 20th century will be one in which widespread suspension of civil liberties only happens, like, three times&quot;. Nope, fucking revolution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's bitter for what seems to be no reason other than pettiness.</div> </div> </div> </div>This lies somewhere teetering between &quot;no he isn't&quot; and &quot;who cares&quot;. Like, again &quot;pettiness&quot; as a driver of grand events is kind of the basis of epic mythology and good melodrama. These are rich and legitimate genres, with meaningful intellectual depth and emotional resonance, especially for people willing to turn off their cynical filters for a second.<br /> <br /> Stuff like this is what turns the original Disney Beauty and the Beast into the goddamn live-action version.<br /> <br /> * Incidentally, if the entire posting history of yourself was available to peruse, I doubt it would be difficult to find you making some of those complaints as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T18:26:20-07:00","id":1297409,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar108_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"108\" data-vbnamecard=\"108\">Flare</a> Seriously, I think outside of the entry in the core that just says Rakan and the Get exist and that they are considered threats by the Sids and Yu-shan the most we've had on him is a bit in the Lunar book. Mind said part literally says that the Silver Pact might have considerd allying with the Get owing to the Gets emnity towards the Sids, but they don't because Rakan is the Get's boss and they don't trust him since he was one of the Sids from the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> Other than that I mean, Rakan is powerful. Yes, he's an elder Sidereal elder exalts are bloody scary because of how powerful they are. The Get view him as their boss. Well yeah, but we don't actually know anything about that relationship. For all we know the Get only serve under because he knows the most about Yu-shan and its agents and the Get view working for him towards that shared goal as the best option for now. Hell even the thing about him doing all the stuff because he views Fate as having cheated him out of his relationship is only known in the explanatory sense. We know that he views his life was a script by someone else and that he despises those he feels responsible for the cruelties of his life, but that's it. We don't know if Rakan wants to burn the system down and remove any trace of the influences of Fate, we don't know if he wants to usurp control of it to give himself and his the lives they believe are owed to them, we don't know if they are just fighting a war because they believe destiny is held by hands too alien to consider a better way of doing things. Certainly not enough that I could even consider using him in a game let alone him being the same plot warping force of a new primordial showing up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T18:29:13-07:00","id":1297411,"title":"","content":"everything I put in there is stuff that was referenced, if not in the books, then stuff outside the books said by the developers, either the old ones or the current ones.<br /> <br /> So if you think I'm making stuff up or whatever, well...I'm not? I'm just aware of what's been said about him.<br /> <br /> Call it incomprehensible if you want though, I guess? Have fun with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T18:46:24-07:00","id":1297414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297356#post1297356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: also excuse me for being confused but how did a topic about Lilith turn into one about Rakan Thulio</div> </div> </div> </div>Because someone trying to argue that there wasn't anything gendered in Lilith's backstory referenced him, leading somebody else to respond with (and I'm paraphrasing here) the &quot;incel LOL&quot; take on the character, and as conceited as it may be, I swear to God, doing my level best to help this be the Exalted Edition that doesn't become inundated with simplified meme renditions of the whole setting and all of its characters is the hill I will die on.<br /> <br /> You will find me there, propping that flag up with my stiffening, blood-soaked hands, and I will reach out and drag you close so that my final breath can be given to convey my last will and testament that that work be carried on.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T18:55:13-07:00","id":1297417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297414#post1297414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because someone trying to argue that there wasn't anything gendered in Lilith's backstory referenced him, leading somebody else to respond with (and I'm paraphrasing here) the &quot;incel LOL&quot; take on the character, and as conceited as it may be, I swear to God, doing my level best to help this be the Exalted Edition that doesn't become inundated with simplified meme renditions of the whole setting and all of its characters is the hill I will die on.<br /> <br /> You will find me there, propping that flag up with my stiffening, blood-soaked hands, and I will reach out and drag you close so that my final breath can be given to convey my last will and testament that that work be carried on.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You're such a martyr.<br /> <br /> Maybe I shouldn't have responded to that in this thread but you were the one that jumped to his defense, with the same tactic you always do, which is fair at least, of 'Well actually he's just being Classically heroic', and my response is to point out that that shit doesn't matter in the context of everything else about him, because the issues with his motivation are, to me at least, borne out of the fact there's a lot of shit wrong with his presentation as a whole, but the fact you can continue to bang on 'classically heroic' may be accurate, but it isn't really acknowledging the entire situation and is instead breaking it down into just a single aspect of the character. My point, and this is why your 'lol incel' snip is inaccurate, is that there is more then a single point here, more then a single action and more then a single observation, and it's not really taking the full judgement when you reduce all arguments against him to 'you're just meming about him being an incel'<br /> <br /> but like, that's fine, I guess?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T19:44:58-07:00","id":1297421,"title":"","content":"The comic being non-canon is kinda big now that I double check what else has been said about him is still canon. The fact that, in it, he pretty clearly still puts blame on the guy who turned him down to the point he is harassing his successor over it like a creepy stalker ex-boyfriend makes it look like he just got turned down for real and he is mad heaven pulled no strings for him to help him get him. Its definitely not the actions of a guy who later found out 'it totally wasn't their fault it was fate ninja fuckery' unless he is just completely insane and doesn't care it wasn't actually their decision because 'if he loved me fate ninja fuckery wouldn't have been enough to make him say no'. But without it being canon it instead becomes entirely possible he solely blames Heaven and maybe someone really did pull some sort of Shun the Smiling Lady fuckery because we don't know anything about how he views the actual target of his affection now since nothing has been said on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T19:59:45-07:00","id":1297423,"title":"","content":"You know, &quot;he loved him so much he had to kill him to make sure nobody else would love him as much&quot;, in the context of the setting's mythology, can easily be read as a Sidereal viewing the magnetism of a Solar as one of the things that makes them so incredibly dangerous to the world, and why they need to be put down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T20:03:25-07:00","id":1297424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297417#post1297417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's not really taking the full judgement when you reduce all arguments against him to 'you're just meming about him being an incel'</div> </div> </div> </div>Not the full argument, just the most infuriating one which introduced it to this thread.<br /> <br /> I literally cannot read your reasons for disliking the character, because trying to make out those enormous blocks of text genuinely hurts my eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T20:20:40-07:00","id":1297428,"title":"","content":"Gonna break this down over multiple posts as best I can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297400#post1297400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Because the second a Getimien shows up, Rakan Thulio has to show up, and the second that Rakan Thulio shows up, the game has to be about him from then on.</div> </div> </div> </div>All right, so this is begging two questions; why does Rakan need to micromanage the Getimians, and why does the game need to be all about him?<br /> <br /> Or at least, any more than a game including a Dynast or Lunar adherent needs to draw in their elders, and how important do those need to be?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rakan Thulio is toxic to the entire system of Exalted because of the way he works and who he is. He is a single person who we are repeatedly told is a big deal, and whenever there is a chance, they tell us how cool he is and what he's done.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is technically, accurate, but for how it disregards the fact that the chances for him to show up are... twice. I'll check later to see if he's mentioned at all in Arms or What Fire Has Wrought.<br /> <br /> And of those two occasions, one of them is to just point out that he's a deal-breaker for Lunars working with Getimians, which is more about Usurper Sidereals as a whole.<br /> <br /> What are his powers that are so overwhelming? He's immortal when Sidereals aren't supposed to be, and he's got something weird to do with Fate. That's about it.<br /> <br /> Do you not think the Lunar elders give a good impression about how much of a challenge a single old Exalt is meant to be.<br /> <br /> For that matter, when are we <i>not</i> told that somebody with a name in the setting is a big deal?<br /> <br /> Last point for now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rakan Thulio has an entire splat of Exalts at his beck and call, apparently almost perfectly to the point that one of the Getimen's key plot points is 'getting away from Rakan Thulio'. This is 2E Deathlords and non-fanon Yozi writ-large; a massively powerful being who can do whatever he wants to you and you are brainwashed into listening to him.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need to be brainwashed to have a very deep connection to somebody, and getting away in an emotional, psychological respect does not need to entail him being within arm's reach of every last one of them, or managing them down to the finest detail.<br /> <br /> Again, this is basically the relationship most Dynasts have with their parents and matriarchs; why don't you see them in this light?<br /> <br /> EDIT: As a start on the other portion of the post, a lot of these complaints about Rakan emerge from how he was talked about by the previous developers. Now isn't the place to do a post-mortem on their stance as developers, but the point is they're gone now, and a number of their ideas and expressions have gone with them.<br /> <br /> I cannot recall if there is something Eric or Vance has said that specifically aligns Getimians with those old statements about how big a deal Thulio is to them.<br /> <br /> EDIT EDIT: Mind, even if the characterisation did still apply, there's a case to be made about how it was and is less about propping him up, and more about creating a compelling source of character drama for the Getimians, as is inherent to every single Exalt type but the Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 03-16-2019, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T20:24:32-07:00","id":1297429,"title":"","content":"Well, this is again solely in respect to the comic version since thats what I was talking about in my original post. I could buy that if he had stopped at just killing the guy he loved in particular but he also went well out of his way to put a giant Creation spanning magical hit out on one solar out of many solely for having the same exaltation centuries later (which of course would also include having first gone out of his way to even figure out which solar got it in the first place and what they looked like so they could put out said hit on that one particular solar thats logically no more magnetic then any of the others out there). Does that really strike you as a guy who did it just because 'man solars sure are scary with all that magnetism I better get rid of the one ensnaring me' instead of the actions of some guy so bitter about being shot down that he is trying to destroy anything even remotely connected to the legacy of the person that dared to turn them down even well after the event happened? If it was really just the magnetism why would he have bothered to find out who is his reincarnation in the first place and in doing so open himself up to possible feelings of some sort to an exalt he might never meet based solely on that connection?<br /> <br /> But this is all moot since the comic is not canon and so his characterization in it as going well out of his way to find out who got his lovers exaltation then harass the specific solar that got his loves exalation is of dubious use in determining his character or how much he blames the person who turned him down vs how much he blames heaven and fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T20:51:45-07:00","id":1297431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297428#post1297428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EDIT: As a start on the other portion of the post, a lot of these complaints about Rakan emerge from how he was talked about by the previous developers. Now isn't the place to do a post-mortem on their stance as developers, but the point is they're gone now, and a number of their ideas and expressions have gone with them.<br /> <br /> I cannot recall if there is something Eric or Vance has said that specifically aligns Getimians with those old statements about how big a deal Thulio is to them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think there's a discussion here on the fact that Rakan Thulio is clearly still going to be important, since Vance specifically brought up 'we want people to be able to be Rakan Thulio's Ex-Lover' and he's still in Lunars. It's very similar to Lilith's looking for her ancient love, so I would argue that at the least there is still the idea that he's supposed to be as important as Lilith, but Lilith wasn't also in the comic and also in the core book; so he's clearly, to me, meant to be more important then Lilith.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297428#post1297428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All right, so this is begging two questions; why does Rakan need to micromanage the Getimians, and why does the game need to be all about him?<br /> <br /> Or at least, any more than a game including a Dynast or Lunar adherent needs to draw in their elders, and how important do those need to be?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Rakan Thulio has to micromange, but I do know that it was said before that a big part of a Getimian's story will be 'escaping' from Thulio- or it was before-, which is why he's important; in terming it as 'escaping' or similar, there are apparently deliberate similarities invoked to Renegade Abyssals and Renegade Infernals; escaping from a massive power. While Dynasts escaping from their parents to rebel against the Realm may be similar, I feel that the scale is different in what they can accomplish. It may not be actively different, and may have more similarities then differences, but this sort of rebellious break from society seems easier for a Dragonblooded, who, while maybe not liked in all corners of the world, can generally find a place that will at least accept them. A Lunar never has to 'escape' their teacher. A Dragonblooded might have to escape their family, but the implication also seems to be if the Dragonblooded is rebellious or otherwise a troublemaker to a point that they can't be fixed, they're generally going to be put aside rather then pressured into a mold. A Dragonblooded is presented as a hero who can do great things, even if their family is problematic or a struggle.<br /> <br /> He is not mentioned in Arms or Fire, but he has been in the first piece of new 3E Media, and then in both the Core and the newest Splat Book.<br /> <br /> I think when you sell a character as hard as Rakan Thulio was sold, the game warps around them. By a reversial of the question; why do games featuring Infernals need to almost always end up focusing on the Yozis? Why were the Deathlords so important in 2e? And the answer is because the narrative weight assigned to those individuals far outstrips other antagonists. By talking about something, it becomes important, and as something is talked about more, it becomes more important.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297428#post1297428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gonna break this down over multiple posts as best I can.<br /> <br /> Do you not think the Lunar elders give a good impression about how much of a challenge a single old Exalt is meant to be.<br /> <br /> For that matter, when are we <i>not</i> told that somebody with a name in the setting is a big deal?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting question, and I think one way to talk about it is to point out the Lunar book.<br /> <br /> How often do they talk about First Age Elders, how often do they speak of what they do? We have Lilith, Ma-Ha-Suchi, Leviathan, and Raksi. But even the text often says that First Age Lunars are working on plans far beyond the short span of years, that they're embroiled in long schemes and thoughts, they talk of these handful of people who are so busy scheming and thinking they often seem to do little- though they are working on their own plots-, and are more concerned with those plots then helping the pact. They take students, but they are not easy to rouse from their plans to HELP you.<br /> <br /> Then they speak of none of the Lunars of the Divine Revolution being alive.<br /> <br /> But, Rakan Thulio is alive. And he is one of the first Exalts, with all the power that entails, and he is not passive, he is active. He is not withdrawn from support and working on distant plans, he has 100 (or so?) Exalts specifically working towards his own goals, which are progressing and which he is working.<br /> <br /> There may be ancient Lunars, but the way Rakan Thulio is presented is utterly different, not just on the timescale, but also on their focus. While Ma-Ha-Suchi wonders if this has been worth all of this suffering, and other ancients plot out their shadow wars against the Bronze Faction or any other number of things, Rakan Thulio by himself and with his Exalts fights the Bronze Faction in an active thing, something called a War, even. His presence is not the ancient thinker who hibernates and plays at games thousands of years in the making, but someone who is here, and he is here to upend the world, like he has been the entire time. The presentation is different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":108,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","user":"Flare","date":". 03-16-2019, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T21:02:08-07:00","id":1297434,"title":"","content":"You are going to have to remind me where it has been said that Rakan is anymore active 'in the field' then other exalted elders who have reached a point where they tend to be more effective by leading and leaving (most of) the field work up to younger exalts. Or where he is 'by himself with just him and his exalts' instead of also seeking recruits from other places like Lunars recruit mortals and spirits to their cause.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T21:09:17-07:00","id":1297436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297434#post1297434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are going to have to remind me where it has been said that Rakan is anymore active 'in the field' then other exalted elders who have reached a point where they tend to be more effective by leading and leaving (most of) the field work up to younger exalts. Or where he is 'by himself with just him and his exalts' instead of also seeking recruits from other places like Lunars recruit mortals and spirits to their cause.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean I don't doubt he has other Exalts? It's just that the Getimiens are the ones that are specifically mentioned. The idea he might actually have even more people on his side isn't exactly saying he's less dangerous though?<br /> <br /> As for his activity, well, there's the whole 'war' thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T21:20:59-07:00","id":1297440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297436#post1297436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean I don't doubt he has other Exalts? It's just that the Getimiens are the ones that are specifically mentioned. The idea he might actually have even more people on his side isn't exactly saying he's less dangerous though?<br /> <br /> As for his activity, well, there's the whole 'war' thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but its a different kind of danger then the 'oh my god these guys are just unstoppable monsters so singularly powerful it warps the whole setting around them' type danger 2E deathlords you are comparing him to had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T21:28:24-07:00","id":1297441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297440#post1297440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but its a different kind of danger then the 'oh my god these guys are just unstoppable monsters so singularly powerful it warps the whole setting around them' type danger 2E deathlords you are comparing him to had.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is at all? In fact my entire point is that it seems like he literally does warp the setting around him even without him having much information because of the information we do have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T21:40:50-07:00","id":1297443,"title":"","content":"I mean, not really. He doesn't even <i>figuratively</i> warp the setting around himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T21:40:57-07:00","id":1297444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think it is at all? In fact my entire point is that it seems like he literally does warp the setting around him even without him having much information because of the information we do have. </div> </div> </div>Having an army is completely different from being someone that, as written, could have personally torn Creation apart by themselves and were only stopped from doing so by being a bunch of chickens that were worried 'what if we somehow mess up and end up like the First and Forsaken Lion or worse at the hands of my angry master' or just weren't actually interested in doing so and were seeing how long they could play at being invincible god kings of death until the Neverborn stopped being satisfied with token efforts involving telling their minions to do things instead of doing it themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T21:48:04-07:00","id":1297446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297414#post1297414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because someone trying to argue that there wasn't anything gendered in Lilith's backstory referenced him, leading somebody else to respond with (and I'm paraphrasing here) the &quot;incel LOL&quot; take on the character, and as conceited as it may be, I swear to God, doing my level best to help this be the Exalted Edition that doesn't become inundated with simplified meme renditions of the whole setting and all of its characters is the hill I will die on.<br /> <br /> You will find me there, propping that flag up with my stiffening, blood-soaked hands, and I will reach out and drag you close so that my final breath can be given to convey my last will and testament that that work be carried on.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I will point out this hilarious because my intention with the joke was, &quot;Do you think you might have overreacted a bit?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297441#post1297441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it is at all? In fact my entire point is that it seems like he literally does warp the setting around him even without him having much information because of the information we do have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not seeing it. The only plots I see where he wraps anything around himself are the Get ,because him being in charge is the most concrete thing we have on them, and Sids owing to him being a rogue elder leading a faction meant specifically to be their special enemies. A Dragonblood game where he shows up i'd need to do a fair amount of setup for my group not to use info they get on him as a bargaining chip to get more direct aid from Sids or Gods before writing him off as someone else's problem. The other ones the best case I'd see would be a non-agression pact owing that they probably wouldn't have anyone they could meaningfully leverage the information on without a high risk of the Johnson trying to kill them afterwords. Heck even a Sid game is hardly warped around him aside from any given suspect list for a string of suspicious activities and problems will invariably have him on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T22:02:01-07:00","id":1297454,"title":"","content":"A big thing to know about Rakan's war against Heaven is that it's also not like like the war Lunars have against the Realm. The gist I got is that Rakan sort of fills in the role of spy agency head/kung fu school sifu. Rakan's war on Heaven looks, in my mind, a lot more like the KGB and the CIA going at eachother, than it does some big world-wide conflict where things are defined and broken day to day in major ways. It's secret, it's in the shadows, and for a lot of the other players, you can probably not even bring it up as the consequences are only relevant to them as plot demands.<br /> <br /> Rakan's main thing, right now, is that he allows the introduction of a new kind of Exalt and puts an extra pile of problems on the Sidereal plate. But that's....it. Getimians havent' been presented as any mor eimpactful than the other bunch of Exalts showing up and messing shit up. I'd say for a lot of Creation, Solars, their derivitives and mroe Exigents is probably much more somehting that's on folks' midns.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T22:05:21-07:00","id":1297455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297431#post1297431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's a discussion here on the fact that Rakan Thulio is clearly still going to be important, since Vance specifically brought up 'we want people to be able to be Rakan Thulio's Ex-Lover' and he's still in Lunars. It's very similar to Lilith's looking for her ancient love, so I would argue that at the least there is still the idea that he's supposed to be as important as Lilith, but Lilith wasn't also in the comic and also in the core book; so he's clearly, to me, meant to be more important then Lilith.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not reasonable to see him as more important because he showed up in the comic, though. The comic is nothing. The comic is cotton candy, a bid of fluff to provide people with a taster while they're waiting for the core book to come out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Rakan Thulio has to micromange, but I do know that it was said before that a big part of a Getimian's story will be 'escaping' from Thulio- or it was before-, which is why he's important; in terming it as 'escaping' or similar, there are apparently deliberate similarities invoked to Renegade Abyssals and Renegade Infernals; escaping from a massive power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I'm going to break down why I think Rakan Thulio exists in the game.<br /> <br /> First of all, when he was first mentioned, I found that he basically existed as a footnote in the wider description of the Getimian Exalted, basically just a plot device for why they exist in the setting. As time went by, he had to accumulate more details as a character in his own right, because that's kind of helpful for any character in the game; that they're well-rounded, including qualities that might associate them with conflict separate from their main political interests.<br /> <br /> The function I see Rakan as originally serving is providing the Getimian Exalted with an elder Exalt mentor, when they otherwise wouldn't have one. I think it felt necessary to give them one, because something that sets basically all of the Exalted apart from the core Solars is in them having some already established society amongst themselves, which even the Abyssals and Infernals get; Liminals don't, but their manner of alienation is its own thing (Exigents don't because they're almost all a community of One). In that he needed to accumulate a few details to explain why a Sidereal would be with these people antithetical to Sidereals, so it would appear that, following the cosmological basis for Getimians being a thing, he's a Sidereal who is in opposition to the rest because of matters pertaining to Destiny rather than Solars.<br /> <br /> I think that's an interesting concept. I think there's compelling drama in the idea of a Sidereal who is broken from the Fellowship owing to matters of Destiny in its own right, and particularly as a basis for what connects him to the Getimian Exalted, in which having been screwed over by Destiny is their whole thing. Noting the likely fact that Rakan's ideals exist for the sake of Getimians, and not the other way around.<br /> <br /> Because Exalted generally need some friction with their elders, it would appear to me that the intent was that Rakan presents a bit of a problematic mentor for Getimians; he has a lot of experience and insight that is very useful for them, but it may also prove that he's an authority figure and control freak (still a Sidereal) in a manner that might grate with their issues with how Destiny has used them, and that some may feel as though they're not really being trained to shine in their own right, but exploited to fulfil Rakan's vendetta. I think these points were and are intended to be written ambiguously. I think the idea of escaping Rakan was not in a literal sense (although doing so probably isn't the hardest thing in the world, since we've got Lunars and Solars to attest to the point that Sidereals with more resources than Rakan can't track down everybody they want dead all the time), but a question of emotions (he probably ought to come across as compelling and helpful to Getimians to fulfil his narrative function), and uncertainty about whether they can hack it on their own (yet).<br /> <br /> If, when the Getimians are written, Rakan is meant to be a side character for them, I find it a lot more likely that he's written as a target or complication to deal with than a cage they can't get free from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Dynasts escaping from their parents to rebel against the Realm may be similar, I feel that the scale is different in what they can accomplish. It may not be actively different, and may have more similarities then differences, but this sort of rebellious break from society seems easier for a Dragonblooded, who, while maybe not liked in all corners of the world, can generally find a place that will at least accept them. A Lunar never has to 'escape' their teacher. A Dragonblooded might have to escape their family, but the implication also seems to be if the Dragonblooded is rebellious or otherwise a troublemaker to a point that they can't be fixed, they're generally going to be put aside rather then pressured into a mold. A Dragonblooded is presented as a hero who can do great things, even if their family is problematic or a struggle.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I take your implication correctly about the problem being that Getimians have trouble fitting in, that seems a lot more about creating drama for them than anything to do with Rakan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">why do games featuring Infernals need to almost always end up focusing on the Yozis?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because their Charms were character bios for the Yozis, their own book talked more about Yozi plans than who they were as people, and there was a follow up book in which they were merely soldiers in the scene of a Yozi to escape, which was presented as being able to succeed.<br /> <br /> That is all way more than we currently have about Rakan, and the assumption that anything else would be written like that strikes me as extremely uncharitable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why were the Deathlords so important in 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because a bunch of them were Essence 10, they had all Solars Charms (including ridiculous ones from Dreams) and a few Sidereal Martial Arts, and the Abyssals book went on and on about them.<br /> <br /> And the answer is because the narrative weight assigned to those individuals far outstrips other antagonists. By talking about something, it becomes important, and as something is talked about more, it becomes more important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, Rakan Thulio is alive. And he is one of the first Exalts, with all the power that entails</div> </div> </div> </div>What power does that entail?<br /> <br /> Look at the way Lunar elders are written now, and apply it to Sidereals; for all intents and purposes, Rakan Thulio is an Essence 5 Sidereal with a few gimmicks (some of which might well be occupied by his immortality and his power over his own Fate).<br /> <br /> The developers have consistently said that no one Exalt is supposed to be singularly enormous within the scope of the setting, but your objection seems particularly based on disregarding that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">he is not passive, he is active. He is not withdrawn from support and working on distant plans, he has 100 (or so?) Exalts specifically working towards his own goals, which are progressing and which he is working.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are all your assumptions, and they don't even seem to be particularly accounting for the setting as it has been written in three books now.<br /> <br /> His situation as a rebel against Heaven would sure seem to withdraw him from a lot of support and resources, it's possible that few to none of his Exalts are above Essence 3, and if they're functioning in about the same manner as Sidereals, they need to act with all of the subtlety that the actual Sidereals need to, without the benefit of things like Yu-Shan gates and allied war gods and elemental dragons and all the riches of Heaven.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There may be ancient Lunars, but the way Rakan Thulio is presented is utterly different, not just on the timescale, but also on their focus. While Ma-Ha-Suchi wonders if this has been worth all of this suffering, and other ancients plot out their shadow wars against the Bronze Faction or any other number of things, Rakan Thulio by himself and with his Exalts fights the Bronze Faction in an active thing, something called a War, even. His presence is not the ancient thinker who hibernates and plays at games thousands of years in the making, but someone who is here, and he is here to upend the world, like he has been the entire time. The presentation is different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're selling the Lunar elders short, not least for disregarding the Shogunate era-ones who are more important, also seem to think that if Ma-Ha-Suchi was out in the world he'd be this massively transformative force all on his own, when... look at his stats, and your picture of Thulio seems determined to not place him in the context of the setting as it is written.<br /> <br /> You presume that he's not only there to upend the world, and that he can actually do so with ease, and yet there the world is, distinctly not upended. Oh sure, once we get a book talking about him, he'll probably be given some feats, but those are the feats of one Exalt amidst hundred of other Celestials and thousands of Terrestrials.<br /> <br /> Sure it's called a war. Lots of things get called wars; my country's fight for independence, for instance. It wasn't a war entailing large, heavily equipped armies doing battle with the British, because we didn't have any of that shit. It had to be focused and subtle, based on maximizing carnage with limited resources. It was also kind of undermined by internal disputes concerning its leadership as a result of things like feeling threatened about who was the most popular, so there's some more for the pedigree of pettiness.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T22:07:40-07:00","id":1297457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297441#post1297441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it is at all? In fact my entire point is that it seems like he literally does warp the setting around him even without him having much information because of the information we do have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point to <i>one</i> thing that is a result of him.<br /> <br /> Not in the abstract, a distinct, described achievement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T22:10:37-07:00","id":1297458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297446#post1297446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will point out this hilarious because my intention with the joke was, &quot;Do you think you might have overreacted a bit?&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>When 900 years old you are, look as good you will not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T22:19:29-07:00","id":1297460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297458#post1297458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When 900 years old you are, look as good you will not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm willing to settle for this at good at 700 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <img src=\"https://i.warosu.org/data/tg/img/0355/71/1413502165954.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Also more on with the present topic of discussion, Rakan hasn't even been given a win condition or a goal yet. The Infernals had the release of the Yozi, who due to their own power them getting out was pretty much an auto-win for their side, in addition to the bit where everything about the Infernals revolved around the Yozi until you swallowed the scorpion and started working to become your own Primordial. And the Deathlords all had these &quot;Any day now [X] will come to fruition&quot; at which point the world would end or the Deathlord would become some nigh-unstoppable force and so on and so forth. Rakan, the closest we've got is a general supposition from the fanbase that he and his are probably aiming to destroy The Loom and that would probably be bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 03-17-2019, 01:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T03:10:09-07:00","id":1297485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297460#post1297460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm willing to settle for this at good at 700 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>We don't all have Seinfeld money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T07:30:30-07:00","id":1297507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297455#post1297455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not reasonable to see him as more important because he showed up in the comic, though. The comic is nothing. The comic is cotton candy, a bid of fluff to provide people with a taster while they're waiting for the core book to come out.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is really unfair to present it like that. I think that while the Comic may have been 'fluff', I think that it's intended to introduce Thulio as a main antagonist to Exalted, and I think saying 'oh it's meaningless' is kinda silly. It's not meaningless. It exists and has what's in it because it wants to define things a certain way. People aren't stupid, people think about why things happen, and to dismiss the idea that the very first part of Exalted 3E's published work focuses so heavily on Rakan Thulio is really questionable; it wasn't just random that he was picked for that spot over someone else, it was intentional. They wanted to introduce us to Exalted 3E, and Exalted 3E is Rakan Thulio, or at least heavily features him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297455#post1297455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, I'm going to break down why I think Rakan Thulio exists in the game.<br /> <br /> First of all, when he was first mentioned, I found that he basically existed as a footnote in the wider description of the Getimian Exalted, basically just a plot device for why they exist in the setting. As time went by, he had to accumulate more details as a character in his own right, because that's kind of helpful for any character in the game; that they're well-rounded, including qualities that might associate them with conflict separate from their main political interests.<br /> <br /> The function I see Rakan as originally serving is providing the Getimian Exalted with an elder Exalt mentor, when they otherwise wouldn't have one. I think it felt necessary to give them one, because something that sets basically all of the Exalted apart from the core Solars is in them having some already established society amongst themselves, which even the Abyssals and Infernals get; Liminals don't, but their manner of alienation is its own thing (Exigents don't because they're almost all a community of One). In that he needed to accumulate a few details to explain why a Sidereal would be with these people antithetical to Sidereals, so it would appear that, following the cosmological basis for Getimians being a thing, he's a Sidereal who is in opposition to the rest because of matters pertaining to Destiny rather than Solars.<br /> <br /> I think that's an interesting concept. I think there's compelling drama in the idea of a Sidereal who is broken from the Fellowship owing to matters of Destiny in its own right, and particularly as a basis for what connects him to the Getimian Exalted, in which having been screwed over by Destiny is their whole thing. Noting the likely fact that Rakan's ideals exist for the sake of Getimians, and not the other way around.<br /> <br /> Because Exalted generally need some friction with their elders, it would appear to me that the intent was that Rakan presents a bit of a problematic mentor for Getimians; he has a lot of experience and insight that is very useful for them, but it may also prove that he's an authority figure and control freak (still a Sidereal) in a manner that might grate with their issues with how Destiny has used them, and that some may feel as though they're not really being trained to shine in their own right, but exploited to fulfil Rakan's vendetta. I think these points were and are intended to be written ambiguously. I think the idea of escaping Rakan was not in a literal sense (although doing so probably isn't the hardest thing in the world, since we've got Lunars and Solars to attest to the point that Sidereals with more resources than Rakan can't track down everybody they want dead all the time), but a question of emotions (he probably ought to come across as compelling and helpful to Getimians to fulfil his narrative function), and uncertainty about whether they can hack it on their own (yet).<br /> <br /> If, when the Getimians are written, Rakan is meant to be a side character for them, I find it a lot more likely that he's written as a target or complication to deal with than a cage they can't get free from.<br /> <br /> If I take your implication correctly about the problem being that Getimians have trouble fitting in, that seems a lot more about creating drama for them than anything to do with Rakan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why can't there just be elder Getimian? Or rogue gods seeking to overturn Fate, which already existed in the form of Forbidden Gods on the outskirts of the Bureaucracy, or the massive slum cities in Yu-Shan proper. Why does there have to specifically be this Elder Sidereal with all these other powers?<br /> <br /> As for the Cage stuff, that's something we'll have to see in play, but the way I've read what's been talked about has been way more aggressive in the idea of Thulio's influence as a Cage then you're presenting it as. It may not be the case, but that's how I've read it, and it's difficult to have a discussion when we're reading the same words and coming away with two totally different observations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297455#post1297455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because their Charms were character bios for the Yozis, their own book talked more about Yozi plans than who they were as people, and there was a follow up book in which they were merely soldiers in the scene of a Yozi to escape, which was presented as being able to succeed.<br /> <br /> That is all way more than we currently have about Rakan, and the assumption that anything else would be written like that strikes me as extremely uncharitable.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Because a bunch of them were Essence 10, they had all Solars Charms (including ridiculous ones from Dreams) and a few Sidereal Martial Arts, and the Abyssals book went on and on about them.<br /> <br /> <br /> And the answer is because the narrative weight assigned to those individuals far outstrips other antagonists. By talking about something, it becomes important, and as something is talked about more, it becomes more important.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And you see in this no comparison at all to Rakan Thulio and the Getimiens, in how their write-ups have been given word count, how they are focused on and framed in the pictures involving them, etc.? This is again an example of 'I don't see this thing you're talking about' as I'm pointing at it and going 'it's this thing right here!'. If we're walking away with totally different observations I'm not sure how much use this conversation really is. Because I see all these traits in the current information we've been given about Getimiens and Rakan Thulio; that the Getimiens are the sideshow and the Abyssals to Rakan Thulio's First and Forsaken Lion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297455#post1297455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What power does that entail?<br /> <br /> Look at the way Lunar elders are written now, and apply it to Sidereals; for all intents and purposes, Rakan Thulio is an Essence 5 Sidereal with a few gimmicks (some of which might well be occupied by his immortality and his power over his own Fate).<br /> <br /> The developers have consistently said that no one Exalt is supposed to be singularly enormous within the scope of the setting, but your objection seems particularly based on disregarding that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It seems odd to say 'what power does being an Elder Exalt really give you?'; especially one as old as him. You're looking at massive gaps in generational ability, and unlike those First Age elders, it does not seem like Rakan Thulio hibernates for 100s of years at a time. One time one of my Storytellers pointed out that in age, Anys Syn and Lupo aren't that far apart. But one of those is regarded as the greatest martial artist in Creation, and the other is not really that special, because one was born before the Usurpation and one was born after. The ages, what these people live through, the momentous things they've been a part of all define them, and Rakan Thulio has, in the Lunar Book at least so far, been given the designation that he stands apart from any other; that he is The Eldest, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297455#post1297455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> These are all your assumptions, and they don't even seem to be particularly accounting for the setting as it has been written in three books now.<br /> <br /> His situation as a rebel against Heaven would sure seem to withdraw him from a lot of support and resources, it's possible that few to none of his Exalts are above Essence 3, and if they're functioning in about the same manner as Sidereals, they need to act with all of the subtlety that the actual Sidereals need to, without the benefit of things like Yu-Shan gates and allied war gods and elemental dragons and all the riches of Heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> WAR IN HEAVEN<br /> Rakan Thulio has been at war with Yu-Shan for centuries.<br /> He is far from alone. A handful of Sidereals have bolstered<br /> his ranks, each with their own reasons to betray Heaven.<br /> Collectively, the conspirators bring to bear intimate knowledge<br /> of the divine bureaucracies. They\u2019ve turned the political<br /> landscape of Yu-Shan into a battleground, and the city<br /> itself into the site of a shadow war between those loyal to<br /> the Celestial Bureaucracy and those who wish to see it torn<br /> down. Dissident and outcast gods flock to his banner; in exchange<br /> for their service, Thulio and his allies promise them<br /> new roles in the order to come. </div> </div> </div>It certainly does not seem that despite this idea of a 'lack of resources' he is having trouble matching the Sidereals and Celestial Bureaucracy, this does not look like a rebel who is pestering at the edges but instead someone who is a powerful foe who is competing and significant in threat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297455#post1297455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're selling the Lunar elders short, not least for disregarding the Shogunate era-ones who are more important, also seem to think that if Ma-Ha-Suchi was out in the world he'd be this massively transformative force all on his own, when... look at his stats, and your picture of Thulio seems determined to not place him in the context of the setting as it is written.<br /> <br /> You presume that he's not only there to upend the world, and that he can actually do so with ease, and yet there the world is, distinctly not upended. Oh sure, once we get a book talking about him, he'll probably be given some feats, but those are the feats of one Exalt amidst hundred of other Celestials and thousands of Terrestrials.<br /> <br /> Sure it's called a war. Lots of things get called wars; my country's fight for independence, for instance. It wasn't a war entailing large, heavily equipped armies doing battle with the British, because we didn't have any of that shit. It had to be focused and subtle, based on maximizing carnage with limited resources. It was also kind of undermined by internal disputes concerning its leadership as a result of things like feeling threatened about who was the most popular, so there's some more for the pedigree of pettiness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, my basis is that I think they will continue to do the same thing they have done to Thulio so far, which is spend a lot of focus- even if the passages themselves are small-, on how different, special, and powerful he is in comparison to any 'normal' Exalt, and why he's a massive threat and etc. etc. I do not think this is a strange thing to believe? Generally people do not suddenly change their actions or their plans for someone for no reason at all, usually once something starts it kinda stays roughly the same.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297457#post1297457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Point to <i>one</i> thing that is a result of him.<br /> <br /> Not in the abstract, a distinct, described achievement.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a fucking baffling question that you seem to think is a big Phoenix Wright turn around, so I have to ask, what do YOU think is a 'distinct, described achievement'? Because we've been over several of them.<br /> <br /> Is the Usurpation one? Because he was an architect of it.<br /> Is being the only immortal Sidereal(Exalt? Well Lunars can be immortal sort of) one? Because he is.<br /> Is tearing your thread from the Loom of Fate one? Because he did.<br /> Is apparently finding a group of Exalts no one knew about to aid you in your war one? Because he's got that.<br /> Is being one of the- so far the ONLY- Original Exalted one? Because he's that.<br /> <br /> Do any of those count?<br /> <br /> but in truth, I don't think this is changing anyone's opinions, so I think it's fair to leave it be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":108,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","user":"Flare","date":". 03-17-2019, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T08:16:07-07:00","id":1297512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297507#post1297507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this is really unfair to present it like that. I think that while the Comic may have been 'fluff', I think that it's intended to introduce Thulio as a main antagonist to Exalted, and I think saying 'oh it's meaningless' is kinda silly. It's not meaningless. It exists and has what's in it because it wants to define things a certain way. People aren't stupid, people think about why things happen, and to dismiss the idea that the very first part of Exalted 3E's published work focuses so heavily on Rakan Thulio is really questionable; it wasn't just random that he was picked for that spot over someone else, it was intentional. They wanted to introduce us to Exalted 3E, and Exalted 3E is Rakan Thulio, or at least heavily features him.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then the new developers come, and say that it's not canon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why can't there just be elder Getimian?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because their narrative place is made more distinct by this idea that they're relatively new.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does there have to specifically be this Elder Sidereal with all these other powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because given the typical narrative place of Sidereals, both in what is being subverted (enforcer of Destiny) and what is being maintained (mentor and advisor), having one of them is more interesting.<br /> <br /> Also, it means there's somebody to teach them Sidereal Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Cage stuff, that's something we'll have to see in play, but the way I've read what's been talked about has been way more aggressive in the idea of Thulio's influence as a Cage then you're presenting it as. It may not be the case, but that's how I've read it, and it's difficult to have a discussion when we're reading the same words and coming away with two totally different observations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of that was just John Morke's style of hyping things, for better or for worse. They're a bit of a moot consideration now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you see in this no comparison at all to Rakan Thulio and the Getimiens</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that we've had no Getimian Charms or a book writing the characters up, there has not even yet been a medium in which the comparison could be made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems odd to say 'what power does being an Elder Exalt really give you?'; especially one as old as him. You're looking at massive gaps in generational ability, and unlike those First Age elders, it does not seem like Rakan Thulio hibernates for 100s of years at a time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your read of the First Age Lunars is just plain wrong.<br /> <br /> Raksi and Ma-Ha-Suchi have not been in hibernation for centuries, and the impact that Lilith's situation has on the development of her powers is ambiguous.<br /> <br /> More importantly, you're completely disregarding the sidebar at the beginning of that chapter that establishes that the standard for Exalted power above Essence 5 is &quot;Essence 5, with some 'Charms' that constitute a consolidation of some of their most well-practiced and characteristic tricks&quot;.<br /> <br /> Raksi is the most powerful Exalt written up in Third Edition thus far, and her signature trick is some extra soak and Hardness while she's casting sorcery. She's not exactly going to set the world on fire with that.<br /> <br /> That's all on top of the manner in which the development of Exalted power above Essence 5 is completely in the realms of Storyteller fiat, as well as the fact that the game consistently attributes legendary feats to Exalted who were probably rated between 2 and 4.<br /> <br /> So there's nothing systemic that would guarantee that Rakan Thulio would have an Essence above 5 (even if he probably does), and he's not going to wind up with anything that massively sets him above any other Essence 5 Sidereal.<br /> <br /> Like I said, it could very well be that his characteristic signature power that arises specifically from his distinct age and experience consists solely of him taking his thread out of the Loom, and not being subjected to his Fated death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One time one of my Storytellers pointed out that in age, Anys Syn and Lupo aren't that far apart. But one of those is regarded as the greatest martial artist in Creation, and the other is not really that special, because one was born before the Usurpation and one was born after.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly; these people are defined by their outlooks and the particular things that they've exerted themselves to achieve, not the level of Super Saiyan they've managed to unlock.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It certainly does not seem that despite this idea of a 'lack of resources' he is having trouble matching the Sidereals and Celestial Bureaucracy, this does not look like a rebel who is pestering at the edges but instead someone who is a powerful foe who is competing and significant in threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I'll admit that I had forgotten about the War in Heaven sidebar. It still reads to me, now as it ever did, as presenting Yu-Shan as the setting of a George La Carre novel rather than something that is going to collapse any day now, but it was not informing the arguments I was making before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, my basis is that I think they will continue to do the same thing they have done to Thulio so far, which is spend a lot of focus- even if the passages themselves are small-, on how different, special, and powerful he is in comparison to any 'normal' Exalt, and why he's a massive threat and etc. etc. I do not think this is a strange thing to believe? Generally people do not suddenly change their actions or their plans for someone for no reason at all, usually once something starts it kinda stays roughly the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is an odd thing to respond to my section pointing out how you're not really considering the setting as it's written.<br /> <br /> Also, people don't suddenly change their plans? Are you talking about the writing? Because... the developers are different. There are different plans all over the shop.<br /> <br /> Did you know that the prior developers were planning to do Arms of the Chosen with this whole big overhaul of the Artifact system? And then Vance and Minton were put in charge, and they scrapped all of those ideas and just stuck to the model established by the corebook? That's one example of plans changing multiple times.<br /> <br /> Never mind that one saying &quot;writer plans don't change&quot; (whatever happened to Techniques again?) is disregarding the plans and statements in which writers and developers, past and present, have wanted to keep the setting from buckling under the weight of individuals who are too powerful.<br /> <br /> That doesn't really matter, because Rakan Thulio doesn't need to change to not be what you presume him to be, but it speaks to a fault in the reasoning.<br /> <br /> As for the rest, there is not one word in a published work talking about how powerful he is in comparison to other Exalted. He is attributed a legendary feat, as... almost all of them are. What there is, is the paragraph just below the one you quoted in full, in which the Getimian Exalted are referred to as the most terrifying aspect of the War, and that Rakan believes their prowess to outstrip that of the Sidereals, of which he is still one.<br /> <br /> If one was to go just by what was written in a book, he'd come across less as their indelible master to which they are but mere slaves and pawns, and more like their ultimate hype man.<br /> <br /> A far cry from any prior depictions of the Deathlords, to be sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do any of those count?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only one that could qualify as &quot;warping the whole setting&quot; is the Usurpation, and it still fails to do so around him, because he doesn't have proprietary ownership of that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T08:47:06-07:00","id":1297518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297512#post1297512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only one that could qualify as &quot;warping the whole setting&quot; is the Usurpation, and it still fails to do so around him, because he doesn't have proprietary ownership of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rest of your post isn't that bad but this kind of makes it clear that we're really not going to ever get anywhere because to me you will always have an excuse, and to you I will always have an excuse. Saying starting a war in Heaven by finding some sort of new Anti-Sids or something isn't 'warping the whole setting' is amazing as a basis because it simultaneously goes 'nothing matters in Yu-Shan' plus 'Exalts don't matter' and 'A guy getting Immortality doesn't matter', all of which are...really different from how the setting has been presented.<br /> <br /> I don't think this is worth continuing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T09:16:57-07:00","id":1297522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297518#post1297518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The rest of your post isn't that bad but this kind of makes it clear that we're really not going to ever get anywhere because to me you will always have an excuse, and to you I will always have an excuse. Saying starting a war in Heaven by finding some sort of new Anti-Sids or something isn't 'warping the whole setting' is amazing as a basis because it simultaneously goes 'nothing matters in Yu-Shan' plus 'Exalts don't matter' and 'A guy getting Immortality doesn't matter', all of which are...really different from how the setting has been presented.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that they don't matter, it's that the setting is filled to the brim with shit like that because it's a world containing thousands of larger-than-life demigods.<br /> <br /> Saying the whole setting is warped around Rakan Thulio would seem to imply that he has a hand in everything important that happens in the way that Second Edition started making the Ebon Dragon feel like. If him having any kind of achievement that causes things to happen at all is warping the setting around him, then either warping the setting is not as big a deal as I would have surmised from your general tone, or there's not a reasonable basis for you to say that it's a big deal for this character, but not for everybody else in the setting who does that, including the Scarlet Empress, matriarchs of the Great Houses, about a dozen elder Lunars, several of Rakan's fellow Sidereals, quite a few Guild hierarchs, the Bull of the North, and several Raksha nobles, on top of a litany of deities.<br /> <br /> If Rakan is warping the setting, he's doing it in competition with several other characters who are about as capable of it as he is, which also leaves lots of room in the setting for things to happen that have nothing to do with him except in the most incidental sense owing to general interconnectedness. The Cinder Isles is an area the size of central Asia undergoing a rather significant change as a result of a clash of nations, the presence of a few Lunar Exalted, and the pursuit of some particularly powerful Fair Folk, and nobody down there cares what's going on in Heaven.<br /> <br /> Okay, maybe rising tension would be an underlying factor in why some of the Bronze Tide's gods feel a need to stick it out with their relocated people rather than seek refuge in Yu-Shan, that's no person being an island.<br /> <br /> I do find something telling in the fact that your model required diminishing the character and achievements of the powerful Lunars depicted in the new book, as to make their impact seem less significant than that of Rakan Thulio. Otherwise, he ranks at about the same level of impact and influence as maybe two mid-level shahan-yas combined. <br /> <br /> I mean hey, one of the ancillary texts we're going to get for What Fire Has Wrought is going to elaborate on the War in the West; the prospect that House Peleps might break away and conquer all of those islands is pretty setting warping.<br /> <br /> Now, I will acknowledge that the win condition for Rakan and the Getimians is arguably somewhat more dramatic than that (although shouldn't really end up being more dramatic than matters such as the resolution to the Realm's succession crisis or Lunars managing to definitively defeat their enemies and declare victory, or a chain of significant Solar achievements). Hence, it ought to be commensurately harder. Not something that feels as though it's going to be resolved in the next couple of years.<br /> <br /> And again, he's not alone in being somebody who wants to achieve something that might dramatically overhaul the setting. That's not what the ambitions of all Celestial Exalted need to be, but it's part of the spectrum of what other ones in the setting might wish to and be capable of achieving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T09:53:45-07:00","id":1297530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297507#post1297507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is really unfair to present it like that... People aren't stupid...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's really uncharitable of you to pretend this is Isator's argument.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T13:12:12-07:00","id":1297564,"title":"","content":"So first off I have never read the comic, now I am interested in buying it just to see what all the hoopla is about. But as someone who hasn\u2019t invested time in it I really don\u2019t understand the significances of a piece of ancillary piece of media that isn\u2019t canon. It probably isn\u2019t going to inform the current developer\u2019s characterization Rakan Thulio going forward as they are the ones that declared the comic non-canon.<br /> <br /> We actually by canon sources have precious little about Getimain and just a smidgen more on Rakan Thulio. Are people making a mountain out of a ant hill here? I find the level of catastrophizing when it comes to Rakan Thulio premature.<br /> <br /> I think given some more word count Rakan Thulio could be made into a more nuanced character. Perhaps the loss of his love started him down the path to seeing how corrupt heaven is and how he had perpetuated it? Something that opened his eyes but in his rage instead of becoming an internal reformer he became an external threat instead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T13:16:34-07:00","id":1297567,"title":"","content":"I think dismissing something as 'non-canon' and therefore not relevant is somewhat disingenuous (intentionally or not) considering the psuedo-canon comprising of a hodge podge of multiple editions, dev posts and discord discussions that many discussion on this forum are predicated upon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T14:21:01-07:00","id":1297581,"title":"","content":"Okay, perhaps I can help here.<br /> <br /> There are some pretty notable issues with depictions of Rakan Thulio in the (non-canonical) comic and in previous dev commentary that folks have correctly identified. We're aware of this, and we've discussed how best to handle Rakan to avoid this at pretty considerable length behind the scenes. His precise motivation for prosecuting his war in heaven isn't the one laid out in the comic, and the details of his interpersonal relationships in the First Age aren't the same. I'm happy with what we've done in realizing him, both as a three-dimensional human being, a potential mentor, and a potential antagonist.<br /> <br /> He's also not going to be an all-powerful NPC or writer's pet. You've seen what Essence 6+ Charms look like in the Lunars preview; anything Rakan has in gonna be in the same mold. The protagonists in the war against Heaven are the Getimians, not him.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":22}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T14:30:23-07:00","id":1297583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297581#post1297581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, perhaps I can help here.<br /> <br /> There are some pretty notable issues with depictions of Rakan Thulio in the (non-canonical) comic and in previous dev commentary that folks have correctly identified. We're aware of this, and we've discussed how best to handle Rakan to avoid this at pretty considerable length behind the scenes. His precise motivation for prosecuting his war in heaven isn't the one laid out in the comic, and the details of his interpersonal relationships in the First Age aren't the same. I'm happy with what we've done in realizing him, both as a three-dimensional human being, a potential mentor, and a potential antagonist.<br /> <br /> He's also not going to be an all-powerful NPC or writer's pet. You've seen what Essence 6+ Charms look like in the Lunars preview; anything Rakan has in gonna be in the same mold. The protagonists in the war against Heaven are the Getimians, not him.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T15:05:15-07:00","id":1297589,"title":"","content":"I'm away from my pdf at the moment, but I'm suddenly recalling how the sidebar in the core book doesn't even identify his lost love as a Solar.<br /> <br /> Even I had internalised that notion enough that it never wavered in my arguments concerning him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T15:09:24-07:00","id":1297592,"title":"","content":"I thought it was a mortal. And the idea being that they were in love, until Heaven decided his Fate was something else.<br /> Was it being a Solar from the comic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T15:25:05-07:00","id":1297595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297592#post1297592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was it being a Solar from the comic?</div> </div> </div> </div> In the comic, it was Eternal Nova, inventor of Single Point Shining Into the Void Style, and the first Chosen to awaken Evocations from an artifact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T15:29:45-07:00","id":1297596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297592#post1297592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it was a mortal. And the idea being that they were in love, until Heaven decided his Fate was something else.<br /> Was it being a Solar from the comic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it was. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1296431#post1296431\">From the current Ask the Devs thread</a>, Vance at least wants to leave it open enough that a PC's prior incarnation could have been Thulio's ex-lover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T16:43:02-07:00","id":1297604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297595#post1297595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In the comic, it was Eternal Nova, inventor of Single Point Shining Into the Void Style, and the first Chosen to awaken Evocations from an artifact.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the greatest swordsman to ever live who went his entire life without a single loss in a 1 on 1 fight while having the power to spontaneously awaken the evocations of any sword awesome enough to qualify for evocations (which he told people he could give them the power to do as well but we never found out if he was lying or not on that one because nobody beat him 1 on 1 to earn the right to learn it).<br /> <br /> I will sort of miss his reincarnation a bit though, it amused me that he used a yoyo as a minor part of his fighting style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T18:18:43-07:00","id":1297617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297589#post1297589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm away from my pdf at the moment, but I'm suddenly recalling how the sidebar in the core book doesn't even identify his lost love as a Solar.<br /> <br /> Even I had internalised that notion enough that it never wavered in my arguments concerning him.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair we did have dev confirmation that the person doing the whole Fate bound hit in the comic was Rakan, and since the person the hit was on was our Solar protagonist's prior incarnation it wasn't exactly a puzzle.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2402_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2402\" data-vbnamecard=\"2402\">The Wizard of Oz</a> To be fair the actual sidebar only says that The Sleepwalker's love chose another and he came to believe Heaven had caused him a great injustice. So it can go in a number of ways, from actual manipulation to Rakan just not being their type. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297604#post1297604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the greatest swordsman to ever live who went his entire life without a single loss in a 1 on 1 fight while having the power to spontaneously awaken the evocations of any sword awesome enough to qualify for evocations (which he told people he could give them the power to do as well but we never found out if he was lying or not on that one because nobody beat him 1 on 1 to earn the right to learn it).<br /> <br /> I will sort of miss his reincarnation a bit though, it amused me that he used a yoyo as a minor part of his fighting style.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eh nothing stopping you from using the character, not like most characters are horribly wrapped up in their past lives this time around.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T18:50:38-07:00","id":1297621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297617#post1297617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair we did have dev confirmation that the person doing the whole Fate bound hit in the comic was Rakan, and since the person the hit was on was our Solar protagonist's prior incarnation it wasn't exactly a puzzle.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Dev commentary here meaning the script for the comic in which he's addressed as Rakan Thulio by name? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> To me, this is on the same level as my overlooking the fact that Games of Divinity never refers to Malfeas as then or having ever been the king of the Primordials, even past the point where I was long revising defunct assumptions about Yozis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T07:59:03-07:00","id":1297724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296566#post1296566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I will say while DotFA did go overboard, they didn't shy away from solars becoming monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part monsters, but some of it was just plain boring. That contrast was jarring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T12:39:15-07:00","id":1297790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297724#post1297724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Part monsters, but some of it was just plain boring. That contrast was jarring.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean it was very disappointing in a lot of ways. I think the only objectively good thing was the guidebook to meru.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T13:03:48-07:00","id":1297793,"title":"","content":"Having the book's text in full and in order is very useful.<br /> <br /> For one thing, it lets one see that the Usurpation is written to present that some of the Lunars who died in that event died actually fighting the Solars.<br /> <br /> From which one could reasonably extract that there were indeed some Lunars who morally or personally objected to the Solars along similar lines to the Usurpers.<br /> <br /> There, everybody should be happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T13:27:16-07:00","id":1298186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297793#post1297793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having the book's text in full and in order is very useful.<br /> <br /> For one thing, it lets one see that the Usurpation is written to present that some of the Lunars who died in that event died actually fighting the Solars.<br /> <br /> From which one could reasonably extract that there were indeed some Lunars who morally or personally objected to the Solars along similar lines to the Usurpers.<br /> <br /> There, everybody should be happy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They weren't included in the plotting, because the DBs and Sids weren't sure they could trust them, but once the punches started flying they were like,<br /> &quot;Hell yeah! I've wanted to kill that guy for centuries. OUT MY WAY! HOLD MY BEER!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T14:05:59-07:00","id":1298191,"title":"","content":"There's a bit in Caste Book: Twilight's Dreams of the First Age chapter where a Solar encounters his Lunar mate in bed with a Person of Air, and challenges her to a duel to the death over her infidelity. With recent discussion of things a Lunar might have done in service or opposition to their mate, that scene came back to my mind as the kind of thing that might come up when a Lunar's disapproval of their mate's reign might induce all the people to pick up and abandon their homes and businesses, and the Solar is so outraged that they get into a similar dispute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T22:32:15-07:00","id":1298850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1297355#post1297355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not about mechanics, it's about how an iconic power of the Sidereals just happens to closely aligned with what a defector is accusing them of. Even if the specific Charm was not employed, it's still a thing that Sidereals do to people's relationships.<br /> <br /> All it takes to put them together is a bit of imagination and some reading in good faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, even if Shun wasn\u2019t involved, Invincible Sword Prince and Of The Thousand Daiklave Wings getting together is simply way too cliche to have not been planned. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-02T09:55:53-07:00","id":1316097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1296754#post1296754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The point remains. People in the 1600\u2019s studied events well before the current era and their average life expectancy was half that\u2014 even not accounting for high mortality in youth. It doesn\u2019t matter that most terrestrials don\u2019t make it past 100 the ones that do are the social movers and shakers of the culture and therefore would inform the academic discourse. It\u2019s just not, to me, realistic that this subject wouldn\u2019t come up even though there would be people alive for most of the shogunate and many years of the early realm whose parents or grandparents rememebered the usurpation.<br /> <br /> Also, per the core, the average life expectancy is 250-300 years\u2014 so not sure where less than a hundred is coming from. (Ex3 34)</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a word called propaganda. It is Latin and was made by Romans. We don't know the history of barbarian peoples who clashed with Rome, because Rome wrote history. The Shogunate controlled history. Remember that. Also remember the spectacular catastrophes that befell the Shogunate, how much priceless knowledge of the Realm Before that was lost, to all but gods, and how a very powerful section of Heaven wants to control history. In our histories (humankind), we didn't have a bunch of people with supernatural abilities that controlled history writing and telling, but even so, not much is for instance known of Rome's many foes except what is written by its historians and propaganda makers. I think you therefore is very wrong concerning what is realistic when it comes to knowledge about an era 1400 years ago. There is no internet in Creation after all....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","name":"Magnus K","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-02T10:47:21-07:00","id":1316119,"title":"","content":"You know you're replying to a post made 3 months ago?<br /> <br /> I have no idea what the context of these statements is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-02T11:02:25-07:00","id":1316124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1296519-my-reaction-to-lilith?p=1316119#post1316119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know you're replying to a post made 3 months ago?<br /> <br /> I have no idea what the context of these statements is.</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad, Sorry. I wasn't really aware. Guess I googled Lillith and then the forum came up and I forgot that it was an old thread (one of my players are playing a character which will be Adamani's recent exaltation in my story). Anyway, the context was that the guy I wrote to basically argued that Dragon Blooded and the world in general, should have a better recollection of the Realm Before than what they seemingly had in written canon, and having studied history, I just chimed in and said why I thought that made little sense, since supernatural creatures were actively working against the &quot;memory&quot; of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","name":"Magnus K","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-02T12:18:33-07:00","id":1316136,"title":"","content":"Yeah there's been a lot of necromancy lately and opening by implying JiveX doesn't know what propaganda is really doesn't endear me to this thread's continuation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}